{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/998155-v20-dark-ages-tome-of-secrets-discussion","id":998155,"title":"V20 Dark Ages Tome of Secrets Discussion","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-11-04T02:57:24-07:00","id":998155,"title":"<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/icons/icon10.png\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" alt=\"\" /> V20 Dark Ages Tome of Secrets Discussion","content":"Wow!<br /> <br /> ok, so I'm pretty tough on a lot of white wolf / opp / bns books when I read them but since the pdf for Tome of Secrets was sent out to ks backers I've spent all night reading it and it is damn fantastic! I only found one section I think is really weak but the rest is brilliant and I can see myself using everything from the fiefdom material to the Setite Sorcery in my games. That Setite Sorcery is brilliant and really expands the clan as well as the power. I think what I like best about the book is although it's a book with loads of powers in it each power has a story and a way to link it into a chronicle as a plot, if you know what I mean.<br /> <br /> Would it be possible to know who wrote each section? some of the writers on this one are fucking amazing at their jobs and need a round of applause.<br /> <br /> Have you read it? what stood out? I'd be interested to know if anyone shares my view that minus one power line in particular this book is about as perfect as a wod sourcebook can be.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3241-stannis","name":"Stannis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3241_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"115"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-04T07:19:32-07:00","id":998213,"title":"","content":"Yeah, jam packed full of content and none of it is bad. I'm a bit saddened that Koldunic Sorcery compels the sorcerer toward conflict and rivalry but it makes sense. The necromancy sequela seems pretty harsh and seems like it should really only affect powers which interact with the shroud but again it's not so offensive that it would stop me from loving cappadocians and Giovanni. Path of Skulls is amazing (dat level 5 power yo).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2818-frostfox","name":"FrostFox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2818_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"264"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-04T15:01:06-07:00","id":998453,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FrostFox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/998155-v20-dark-ages-tome-of-secrets-discussion?p=998213#post998213\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, jam packed full of content and none of it is bad. I'm a bit saddened that Koldunic Sorcery compels the sorcerer toward conflict and rivalry but it makes sense. The necromancy sequela seems pretty harsh and seems like it should really only affect powers which interact with the shroud but again it's not so offensive that it would stop me from loving cappadocians and Giovanni. Path of Skulls is amazing (dat level 5 power yo).</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah! it makes perfect sense now why the tzimisce couldn't band together to face off against the fledgling tremere or at least it makes more sense than it did before","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3241-stannis","name":"Stannis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3241_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"115"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-04T18:52:05-07:00","id":998549,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stannis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/998155-v20-dark-ages-tome-of-secrets-discussion?p=998453#post998453\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah! it makes perfect sense now why the tzimisce couldn't band together to face off against the fledgling tremere or at least it makes more sense than it did before</div> </div> </div> </div>It still seems somewhat off....anyone they're teaching Koldunic Sorcery to would also suffer the effects, so the student would always be tempted by the demonic spirits to overthrow their teacher. All Koldunists would know this so they'd be reluctant to take students at all so it wouldn't propagate very well at all and would likely be very personal with Tzimisce having to teach themselves rather than learn from others.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2818-frostfox","name":"FrostFox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2818_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"264"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-05T02:09:33-07:00","id":998660,"title":"","content":"So, the <i>Tome of Secrets</i> is... mediocre. It's not actively bad, like, say, <i>Jerusalem by Night</i>, but it's mostly just special powers for &quot;special&quot; vampires. I really don't have much of a need for additional paths of Sorcery or Necromancy; I actively don't want Lasombra fan service (also known as Abyss Mysticism). There's a rather general lack of specificity in much of the writing. And the section on fiefdoms is terrible, both in terms of writing, and in terms of concepts. Take this passage, for instance:<div style=\"margin-left:40px\"><i>At its heart, a vassalage or feudatory arrangement is a barter of services. Since ancient days when priests would manage rites and calendars in exchange for care and honors to their gods, the terms of duty have expanded, but never truly changed. From the tithe of the temple came the warlord\u2019s tax of grain. From that tax of grain? Armies marched and territories expanded far beyond the reach of one leader to manage. Lands were offered as rewards, and in return? Grain and loyalty. That grain could be called gold, sons to serve, well-forged steel, or any other resource. The core truth of the trade has never changed. For the spoils of the servant? The liege must offer security.<br /> <br /> The feudal societies of medieval Europe honed and codified these practices, empowering local liege lords in the twilight of the imperial legions. Now? The liege stands mighty in the lands he rules, answering only to his liege in turn, and only then against threats beyond his limited reach. Nobles fight amongst themselves, a War of Princes no less savage or cunning than one Cainites have fought in the shadows for millennia. Have they learned these methods from the Damned?<br /> <br /> Or perhaps, are the Laws of Caine simply the oldest, bloodiest example of an ancient truth?<br /> <br /> For the spoils of the kine? The eldest must offer security. One who fails? Dies.</i><br /> </div> That's an example of really bad writing, showing weak communication of concepts, a weak understanding of the concepts which the writer is attempting to communicate, and an appalling use of questions marks.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/317-james_willoughby","name":"James_Willoughby","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar317_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-05T03:32:01-07:00","id":998676,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>James_Willoughby</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/998155-v20-dark-ages-tome-of-secrets-discussion?p=998660#post998660\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, the <i>Tome of Secrets</i> is... mediocre. It's not actively bad, like, say, <i>Jerusalem by Night</i>, but it's mostly just special powers for &amp;quot;special&amp;quot; vampires. I really don't have much of a need for additional paths of Sorcery or Necromancy; I actively don't want Lasombra fan service (also known as Abyss Mysticism). There's a rather general lack of specificity in much of the writing. And the section on fiefdoms is terrible, both in terms of writing, and in terms of concepts. Take this passage, for instance:<div style=\"margin-left:40px\"><i>At its heart, a vassalage or feudatory arrangement is a barter of services. Since ancient days when priests would manage rites and calendars in exchange for care and honors to their gods, the terms of duty have expanded, but never truly changed. From the tithe of the temple came the warlord\u2019s tax of grain. From that tax of grain? Armies marched and territories expanded far beyond the reach of one leader to manage. Lands were offered as rewards, and in return? Grain and loyalty. That grain could be called gold, sons to serve, well-forged steel, or any other resource. The core truth of the trade has never changed. For the spoils of the servant? The liege must offer security.<br /> <br /> The feudal societies of medieval Europe honed and codified these practices, empowering local liege lords in the twilight of the imperial legions. Now? The liege stands mighty in the lands he rules, answering only to his liege in turn, and only then against threats beyond his limited reach. Nobles fight amongst themselves, a War of Princes no less savage or cunning than one Cainites have fought in the shadows for millennia. Have they learned these methods from the Damned?<br /> <br /> Or perhaps, are the Laws of Caine simply the oldest, bloodiest example of an ancient truth?<br /> <br /> For the spoils of the kine? The eldest must offer security. One who fails? Dies.</i><br /> </div> That's an example of really bad writing, showing weak communication of concepts, a weak understanding of the concepts which the writer is attempting to communicate, and an appalling use of questions marks.</div> </div> </div> </div>i find that really interesting because I see abyss mysticism and new necromancy as adding more layers to existing clans.i like options.<br /> <br /> As for the writing in some sections i agree there's a lot of weakness. i found the assimite section really badly written. like you've mentioned on fiefdoms, there's so much weak statements, ambiguity, passivity, and it's like an editor or developer never looked at it, but i accept i may just have high standards. another user i talked to last night really liked the assimite section. but yeah i'd say the assimite content is pretty useless and the fiefdoms content is woolly but in a way that i can use unlike with the assimites.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3241-stannis","name":"Stannis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3241_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"115"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-05T03:34:09-07:00","id":998677,"title":"","content":"on the flip side i love Setite Sorcery, Necromancy, holy things, unholy things, and knights and warfare. The Setite Sorcery in particular is really impressive","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3241-stannis","name":"Stannis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3241_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"115"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-05T05:06:22-07:00","id":998701,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FrostFox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/998155-v20-dark-ages-tome-of-secrets-discussion?p=998549#post998549\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It still seems somewhat off....anyone they're teaching Koldunic Sorcery to would also suffer the effects, so the student would always be tempted by the demonic spirits to overthrow their teacher. All Koldunists would know this so they'd be reluctant to take students at all so it wouldn't propagate very well at all and would likely be very personal with Tzimisce having to teach themselves rather than learn from others.</div> </div> </div> </div>You mean that koldun are basically Sith ? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/redface.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Embarrassment\" smilieid=\"2\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> Joke aside, it explains well why koldunic sorcery is so rare and why it went almost extinct.<br /> I want to read the book now...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12595-nitenshi","name":"Nitenshi","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"110"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-05T06:53:08-07:00","id":998737,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>James_Willoughby</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/998155-v20-dark-ages-tome-of-secrets-discussion?p=998660#post998660\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, the <i>Tome of Secrets</i> is... mediocre. It's not actively bad, like, say, <i>Jerusalem by Night</i>, but it's mostly just special powers for &quot;special&quot; vampires. I really don't have much of a need for additional paths of Sorcery or Necromancy; I actively don't want Lasombra fan service (also known as Abyss Mysticism). There's a rather general lack of specificity in much of the writing. And the section on fiefdoms is terrible, both in terms of writing, and in terms of concepts. Take this passage, for instance:<div style=\"margin-left:40px\"><i>At its heart, a vassalage or feudatory arrangement is a barter of services. Since ancient days when priests would manage rites and calendars in exchange for care and honors to their gods, the terms of duty have expanded, but never truly changed. From the tithe of the temple came the warlord\u2019s tax of grain. From that tax of grain? Armies marched and territories expanded far beyond the reach of one leader to manage. Lands were offered as rewards, and in return? Grain and loyalty. That grain could be called gold, sons to serve, well-forged steel, or any other resource. The core truth of the trade has never changed. For the spoils of the servant? The liege must offer security.<br /> <br /> The feudal societies of medieval Europe honed and codified these practices, empowering local liege lords in the twilight of the imperial legions. Now? The liege stands mighty in the lands he rules, answering only to his liege in turn, and only then against threats beyond his limited reach. Nobles fight amongst themselves, a War of Princes no less savage or cunning than one Cainites have fought in the shadows for millennia. Have they learned these methods from the Damned?<br /> <br /> Or perhaps, are the Laws of Caine simply the oldest, bloodiest example of an ancient truth?<br /> <br /> For the spoils of the kine? The eldest must offer security. One who fails? Dies.</i><br /> </div>That's an example of really bad writing, showing weak communication of concepts, a weak understanding of the concepts which the writer is attempting to communicate, and an appalling use of questions marks.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Ouch. That is pretty bad.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-05T18:49:11-07:00","id":998984,"title":"","content":"Honestly I can kind of see the issue, while I personally love new Settite sorcery and stuff, setites have alot of shiny toys already. What is there for the Ventrue? The Toreador? The Nosferatu? Mortal play is something anyone can buy in on, but magics those are clan only","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-05T19:32:13-07:00","id":999001,"title":"","content":"Well the Tome of Secrets seems to just be a Rites of the Blood for the Dark Ages. The secret sorceries of the Assamites, Setites, Tzimisce, and Lasombra primarily. There's powers that exist for Ventrue, Toreador, and Nosferatu disciplines all over the place but this adds interesting things for Blood Sorceries. I don't want every clan to get Blood Sorceries either. I think the Anarch sorceries in Rites of the Blood are the worst. But then, ever will there be opinions regarding these things and not everyone will be pleased. I am personally pleased with what was in this book, as far as mechanics go.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2818-frostfox","name":"FrostFox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2818_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"264"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-05T19:45:55-07:00","id":999006,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FrostFox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/998155-v20-dark-ages-tome-of-secrets-discussion?p=999001#post999001\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well the Tome of Secrets seems to just be a Rites of the Blood for the Dark Ages. The secret sorceries of the Assamites, Setites, Tzimisce, and Lasombra primarily. There's powers that exist for Ventrue, Toreador, and Nosferatu disciplines all over the place but this adds interesting things for Blood Sorceries. I don't want every clan to get Blood Sorceries either. I think the Anarch sorceries in Rites of the Blood are the worst. But then, ever will there be opinions regarding these things and not everyone will be pleased. I am personally pleased with what was in this book, as far as mechanics go.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Not everyone has to get blood sorceries. That's really a problem in and of itself treating magic as the only &quot;cool secret&quot; a clan can have. This is the tome of Secrets not &quot;The Tome of Lasombra, Assamite, Settite and Capadocian Secrets&quot; Not having anything clan specific for the other clans is in my mind a big gap.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-05T20:17:53-07:00","id":999028,"title":"","content":"To be completely and totally honest, I have no recollection of writing what I wrote, it was really long ago and I was doing a lot at the time. We also haven't been sent our free PDFs, so I can't check. However, if anyone would like historical resources on fiefs (and I did not write that section), I recommend the following links. They're class notes by Richard Abels, who's one of the top twenty Medievalists in the world. They're pretty easy to follow in my opinion, and I recognize they might not be helpful, but I'd like to provide them in case they are. They're outlines, with bolded sections and numbers and everything.<br /> <br /> &quot;Feudalism&quot;:<br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://www.usna.edu/Users/history/abels/hh315/Feudal.htm\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://www.usna.edu/CMS/_standard3.0/_files/img/logo.png\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.usna.edu/Users/history/abels/hh315/Feudal.htm\" target=\"_blank\"> 404 Navigation Error :: USNA </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.usna.edu/Users/history/abels/hh315/Feudal.htm\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.usna.edu/Users/history/abels/hh315/Feudal.htm </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> &quot;Chivalry&quot;:<br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://www.usna.edu/Users/history/abels/hh381/Chivalry.htm\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://www.usna.edu/CMS/_standard3.0/_files/img/logo.png\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.usna.edu/Users/history/abels/hh381/Chivalry.htm\" target=\"_blank\"> 404 Navigation Error :: USNA </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.usna.edu/Users/history/abels/hh381/Chivalry.htm\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.usna.edu/Users/history/abels/hh381/Chivalry.htm </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:12px\">-</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3093-hm8453a","name":"hm8453a","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3093_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"636"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-05T21:05:22-07:00","id":999052,"title":"","content":"You have to remember that this book is a collection of stretch goals that were created specifically to expand on blood magics, holy and unholy things and cainite vassalage. The book delivered exactly what it promised it'd do.<br /> <br /> I dont think one can complain about OPP releasing this book when we helped create it.<br /> <br /> If we'd gotten more strechgoals done maybe we'd have some more non blood magic secrets revealed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imageshack.com/i/j5vvlqp\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/j5vvlqp\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/ghw20supporterhiddengaroup\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/n18segp\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0v25ewp\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">English is not my native language, so i apologize for errors in grammar or spelling.</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/392-cadmiumcadamium","name":"Cadmiumcadamium","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar392_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"936"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-05T22:29:50-07:00","id":999073,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FrostFox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/998155-v20-dark-ages-tome-of-secrets-discussion?p=999001#post999001\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well the Tome of Secrets seems to just be a Rites of the Blood for the Dark Ages. The secret sorceries of the Assamites, Setites, Tzimisce, and Lasombra primarily. There's powers that exist for Ventrue, Toreador, and Nosferatu disciplines all over the place but this adds interesting things for Blood Sorceries. I don't want every clan to get Blood Sorceries either. I think the Anarch sorceries in Rites of the Blood are the worst. But then, ever will there be opinions regarding these things and not everyone will be pleased. I am personally pleased with what was in this book, as far as mechanics go.</div> </div> </div> </div>Anything for Tremere Thaumaturgy in there?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11512-zanos","name":"Zanos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11512_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"550"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-05T23:01:26-07:00","id":999084,"title":"","content":"Fiefdoms, Holy/Unholy Things are my favorite part. Out of all the sorcery Necromancy and Setites are of interest to me. I never play Assamites and hate Lasombra so I'll never use those.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1250-shadowlost","name":"Shadowlost","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1250_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"155"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-05T23:13:20-07:00","id":999086,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zanos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/998155-v20-dark-ages-tome-of-secrets-discussion?p=999073#post999073\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Anything for Tremere Thaumaturgy in there?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Oh is there such a thing in the WoD? I didn't know the Tremere had blood sorcery at their disposal! That must be cool huh... &quot;Tremere Thaumaturgy&quot; hmmmm...I've heard something like this quite some time ago but can't remember the details...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-06T00:26:22-07:00","id":999101,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cadmiumcadamium</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/998155-v20-dark-ages-tome-of-secrets-discussion?p=999052#post999052\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You have to remember that this book is a collection of stretch goals that were created specifically to expand on blood magics, holy and unholy things and cainite vassalage. The book delivered exactly what it promised it'd do.<br /> <br /> I dont think one can complain about OPP releasing this book when we helped create it.<br /> <br /> If we'd gotten more strechgoals done maybe we'd have some more non blood magic secrets revealed.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> the only stretch goal on it that didn't look like we got was extended Witchcraft rules. And honestly I think the book is good for what it is, but i can see if you are a fan of say Ventrue seeing another thing of abyssal mysticism is kind of frustrating.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-06T01:09:45-07:00","id":999107,"title":"","content":"Can someone provide an outline of the content?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Writer, Game Designer, Pro since 99.<br /> <br /> Thoughts at <a href=\"http://mobunited.com\" target=\"_blank\">mobunited.com</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/164-malcolm","name":"Malcolm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar164_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-06T04:10:42-08:00","id":999151,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malcolm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/998155-v20-dark-ages-tome-of-secrets-discussion?p=999107#post999107\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can someone provide an outline of the content?</div> </div> </div> </div>Chapter 2 - Forgotten Sorceries: Abyssal Mysticism, Assasmite Sorcery, Koldunic Sorcery, Necromancy, setite Sorcery and a broad overview of Witchcraft.<br /> <br /> Chapter 3 - The Weight of Nobility: A fairly broad outline of Medieval sociology, economics and warfare, as well as how Cainites fit into that framework.<br /> <br /> Chapter 4 - The Holiest of Things: True Faith, Holy artifacts, biblical necromancy, demonic worship and Dark Thaumaturgy<br /> <br /> Appendix - Some unique combination disciplines.<br /> <br /> <br /> Personally, I really liked The Weight of Nobility. I'm just a sucker for that kind of sociological analysis.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-06T04:27:05-08:00","id":999154,"title":"","content":"There's not even thing about the Malkavian cults ? Shame, I'd like to see more of this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12595-nitenshi","name":"Nitenshi","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"110"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-06T06:37:35-08:00","id":999190,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>James_Willoughby</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/998155-v20-dark-ages-tome-of-secrets-discussion?p=998660#post998660\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I actively don't want Lasombra fan service (also known as Abyss Mysticism).</div> </div> </div> </div>Disregarding all eventual points you had in your post, I do find this sentiment quite... lacking. Someone wrote something about a clan you don't care about? You call it fan service? Well, the whole book IS fan-service. It was written as a stretch goal, as you should know, and focus was said to be on sorceries and stuff. So why this unmotivated lash out on a certain type of content? And those who like that type of content? Just because it's nothing you use?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/deluxe-hunters-hunted-ii\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img692/7017/hh2support.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><a href=\"https://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/deluxe-anarchs-unbound\" target=\"_blank\"> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img703/6636/6kvo.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> <a href=\"https://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/deluxe-mage-the-ascension-20th-anniversary-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img31/2512/25ew.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> <a href=\"https://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/deluxe-w20-book-of-the-wyrm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/507-ignytezero","name":"IgnyteZero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar507_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-06T06:59:20-08:00","id":999202,"title":"","content":"Unlike James_Willoughby, I don't see a problem with the &quot;Lasombra fan service&quot;. The problem I see is that the Tremere get more and more irrelevant in the WoD (perhaps because most tremere players either &quot;went back&quot; to Ars Magica or decided to play Mage after they started to see the process of destroying their clan getting started lol...). In any case, I really appreciate new material for every other blood sorcery, I just don't like the idea of destroying one of the main clans in the history of WoD.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-06T08:47:23-08:00","id":999235,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Herr Meister</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/998155-v20-dark-ages-tome-of-secrets-discussion?p=999202#post999202\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Unlike James_Willoughby, I don't see a problem with the &quot;Lasombra fan service&quot;. The problem I see is that the Tremere get more and more irrelevant in the WoD (perhaps because most tremere players either &quot;went back&quot; to Ars Magica or decided to play Mage after they started to see the process of destroying their clan getting started lol...). In any case, I really appreciate new material for every other blood sorcery, I just don't like the idea of destroying one of the main clans in the history of WoD.</div> </div> </div> </div>i disagree man. the tremere are still unique. they're not just the thaumaturgy clan - they've got history, a unique structure, and a focused role within domains. adding more detail to other clans doesn't take anything away from the tremere.<br /> <br /> dark thaumaturgy's in there anyway and so is witchcraft","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3241,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3241-stannis","user":"Stannis","date":". 11-06-2016, 11:49 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3241-stannis","name":"Stannis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3241_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"115"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-06T08:48:19-08:00","id":999236,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nitenshi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/998155-v20-dark-ages-tome-of-secrets-discussion?p=999154#post999154\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's not even thing about the Malkavian cults ? Shame, I'd like to see more of this.</div> </div> </div> </div>i don't think that was something hit in the dark ages stretch goals so i don't see why it would be in there. maybe ask on the monday meeting notes whether it's in dark ages companion?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3241-stannis","name":"Stannis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3241_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"115"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-06T08:51:04-08:00","id":999238,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/998155-v20-dark-ages-tome-of-secrets-discussion?p=999006#post999006\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Not everyone has to get blood sorceries. That's really a problem in and of itself treating magic as the only &quot;cool secret&quot; a clan can have. This is the tome of Secrets not &quot;The Tome of Lasombra, Assamite, Settite and Capadocian Secrets&quot; Not having anything clan specific for the other clans is in my mind a big gap.</div> </div> </div> </div>i belive dark ages companion contains apocrypha for all the clans from what the blog posts about it said","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3241-stannis","name":"Stannis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3241_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"115"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-06T08:51:55-08:00","id":999239,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zanos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/998155-v20-dark-ages-tome-of-secrets-discussion?p=999073#post999073\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Anything for Tremere Thaumaturgy in there?</div> </div> </div> </div>there's a nice section on dark thaumaturgy and another on witchcraft so that can cover infernal and telyavelic tremere!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3241-stannis","name":"Stannis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3241_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"115"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-06T10:29:04-08:00","id":999297,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Herr Meister</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/998155-v20-dark-ages-tome-of-secrets-discussion?p=999202#post999202\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Unlike James_Willoughby, I don't see a problem with the &quot;Lasombra fan service&quot;. The problem I see is that the Tremere get more and more irrelevant in the WoD (perhaps because most tremere players either &quot;went back&quot; to Ars Magica or decided to play Mage after they started to see the process of destroying their clan getting started lol...). In any case, I really appreciate new material for every other blood sorcery, I just don't like the idea of destroying one of the main clans in the history of WoD.</div> </div> </div> </div>Eh, I disagree that the Tremere are becoming more irrelevant. Just because these things feature so prominently in this book does not mean they are more prevalent. If anything this points out as to why Koldunic Sorcery is as rare as it is. But PCs are usually a bit more speshul than NPCs. The Tremere have institutionalized their magic and every single one of them has it. Abyss Mysticism is rare and largely distrusted even within the Lasombra clan. They are giving up their own ambitions to become tools of the Abyss, essentially. Koldunic Sorcerers are compelled toward rivalry and theft of information from their fellow sorcerers. Assamites are behind the Tremere when it comes to how many of them use Sorcery, and they don't do it as well. Setites are still as distrusted as ever.<br /> <br /> And this -is- the Dark Ages so it's a time when the Tremere are fighting tooth and nail just to survive so they can see the Modern Nights. These powers are all waning in frequency while the Tremere are waxing into their power after all the fighting and wars that still don't manage to wipe these cockroaches out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2818-frostfox","name":"FrostFox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2818_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"264"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-06T10:42:51-08:00","id":999305,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FrostFox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/998155-v20-dark-ages-tome-of-secrets-discussion?p=999297#post999297\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Eh, I disagree that the Tremere are becoming more irrelevant. Just because these things feature so prominently in this book does not mean they are more prevalent. If anything this points out as to why Koldunic Sorcery is as rare as it is. But PCs are usually a bit more speshul than NPCs. The Tremere have institutionalized their magic and every single one of them has it. Abyss Mysticism is rare and largely distrusted even within the Lasombra clan. They are giving up their own ambitions to become tools of the Abyss, essentially. Koldunic Sorcerers are compelled toward rivalry and theft of information from their fellow sorcerers. Assamites are behind the Tremere when it comes to how many of them use Sorcery, and they don't do it as well. Setites are still as distrusted as ever.<br /> <br /> And this -is- the Dark Ages so it's a time when the Tremere are fighting tooth and nail just to survive so they can see the Modern Nights. These powers are all waning in frequency while the Tremere are waxing into their power after all the fighting and wars that still don't manage to wipe these cockroaches out.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is my favourite post of the thread. Perfectly describes the divide in blood sorcerers as I see it.<br /> <br /> I'm glad you appreciate the Koldunic Sorcery too, albeit with reservations about the rivalries it causes. I wrote that, Setite Sorcery, Necromancy, Unholy Things, and Abyss Mysticism.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#000080\">Matthew Dawkins</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000080\">In-House Developer for Onyx Path Publishing</span></b><br /> <br /> <i><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b><span style=\"color:#008080\">Website: </span><a href=\"http://www.matthewdawkins.com\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.matthewdawkins.com</span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#008080\">Patreon: </span><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins</span></a></b></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/152-the-gentleman-gamer","name":"The Gentleman Gamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar152_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-06T11:10:01-08:00","id":999329,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FrostFox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/998155-v20-dark-ages-tome-of-secrets-discussion?p=999297#post999297\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Eh, I disagree that the Tremere are becoming more irrelevant. Just because these things feature so prominently in this book does not mean they are more prevalent. If anything this points out as to why Koldunic Sorcery is as rare as it is. But PCs are usually a bit more speshul than NPCs. The Tremere have institutionalized their magic and every single one of them has it. Abyss Mysticism is rare and largely distrusted even within the Lasombra clan. They are giving up their own ambitions to become tools of the Abyss, essentially. Koldunic Sorcerers are compelled toward rivalry and theft of information from their fellow sorcerers. Assamites are behind the Tremere when it comes to how many of them use Sorcery, and they don't do it as well. Setites are still as distrusted as ever.<br /> <br /> And this -is- the Dark Ages so it's a time when the Tremere are fighting tooth and nail just to survive so they can see the Modern Nights. These powers are all waning in frequency while the Tremere are waxing into their power after all the fighting and wars that still don't manage to wipe these cockroaches out.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Well said, I see your point and I agree. The fact is that I sometimes think that the Tremere need more loving after all that they have suffered and seeing a book about blood sorcery that almost excludes them makes me feel sad for them, you know. But as I stated before, I love all the new material for the different kinds of blood sorcery and I'd welcome even more, I just complained that that part of the Tremere history that was used to justify (and in my case, cause admiration, as I started to like the Tremere after reading about their many innovations and inventive nature, fighting on many fronts and ending up being victorious because of perseverance, geniality etc) their victory against all odds, that is, innovation, organization and sheer brilhance (besides ofc, old rivalries among other clans that would never let them work together to destroy the fledgling clan etc). But, in any way you have explained your point perfectly and I couldn't, even if I wanted to (and it wouldn't be fair!), add anything regarding what you wrote.<br /> <br /> Cheers,<br /> Daniel.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-06T11:26:35-08:00","id":999343,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Gentleman Gamer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/998155-v20-dark-ages-tome-of-secrets-discussion?p=999305#post999305\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This is my favourite post of the thread. Perfectly describes the divide in blood sorcerers as I see it.<br /> <br /> I'm glad you appreciate the Koldunic Sorcery too, albeit with reservations about the rivalries it causes. I wrote that, Setite Sorcery, Necromancy, Unholy Things, and Abyss Mysticism.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, Good Stuff. Definitely a lot of drawbacks added to certain sorceries but nothing absolutely debilitating really. If I had to make an adjustment to how the rivalries worked I'd make it so it's only for outside your Koldunic line or something like that. An easy enough adjustment to make for homebrew. Makes it so that the bond between teacher and student isn't necessarily going to be broken as readily but encourages the infighting between Koldunic lines and adds more fuel for the blood feuds the Tzimisce are known for.<br /> <br /> The Necromancy stuff was good, though I felt that the Sequela affects should only occur with Necromancy paths that interact with the shroud, but again something easy enough to homebrew. Would the Sequela effects have the added benefit of thinning the shroud and thus making things that affect the shroud easier? All of those effects kind of describe the kind of places where the shroud is thinnest.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Herr Meister</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/998155-v20-dark-ages-tome-of-secrets-discussion?p=999329#post999329\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Well said, I see your point and I agree. The fact is that I sometimes think that the Tremere need more loving after all that they have suffered and seeing a book about blood sorcery that almost excludes them makes me feel sad for them, you know. But as I stated before, I love all the new material for the different kinds of blood sorcery and I'd welcome even more, I just complained that that part of the Tremere history that was used to justify (and in my case, cause admiration, as I started to like the Tremere after reading about their many innovations and inventive nature, fighting on many fronts and ending up being victorious because of perseverance, geniality etc) their victory against all odds, that is, innovation, organization and sheer brilhance (besides ofc, old rivalries among other clans that would never let them work together to destroy the fledgling clan etc). But, in any way you have explained your point perfectly and I couldn't, even if I wanted to (and it wouldn't be fair!), add anything regarding what you wrote.<br /> <br /> Cheers,<br /> Daniel.</div> </div> </div> </div>I see the Tremere as a bit more like villains. Certainly they're admirable in their ability to persevere and what they've accomplished but they certainly have behavioral variances. In fact, in most of the fiction they aren't portrayed as genial at all. Etrius is by far the most genial of them I've seen portrayed (with another being Dr. Bainbridge in Victorian Age Vampire trilogy) while most are conniving and lowly in their behavior, some even downright villainous (Anton Wellig). Jervais from Dark Ages Clan Novel Tremere kind of straddles the line on it, really. He's genial but he's also got that conniving two-faced nature, but then again he is of the line of Goratrix.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2818,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2818-frostfox","user":"FrostFox","date":". 11-06-2016, 02:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2818-frostfox","name":"FrostFox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2818_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"264"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-06T11:57:51-08:00","id":999358,"title":"","content":"I see that they have many behavioral variances, but nobody can deny the geniality of a Goratrix (one of my favorite characters in the WoD history, I mean, the guy makes the perfect villain) for instance. I also like Etrius, but he is very different from Goratrix, basically the other side of the coin, too cautious, too meticulous and with that strange &quot;holier than thou&quot; attitude that sounds even more strange when we're talking about usurpers lol. I see the Goratrix line as more lowly and &quot;two-faced&quot; or simply villainous and I'm not a big fan of Jervais, he's just too low! I also love the adventurous Celestyn, he's the kind of tremere everybody wants to be, but he's not a villain at all. But after all, the Tremere that conquered my heart was really Goratrix, the guy who came up with the potion of vampirism, that created the gargoyles, created a kind of artificial blood (although not very efficient lol) and ended up building his own house...oh and I can't forget that he made Tariq a 13th generation vampire, &quot;well deserved loser&quot; hahaha. I think I'd love to see WW develop more of his history, we need &quot;big bad guys&quot; like him. All in all, I like villains (I think almost every ST does lol) and I think the Tremere are great in this role.<br /> <br /> Cheers,<br /> Daniel.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-06T12:14:29-08:00","id":999367,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Herr Meister</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/998155-v20-dark-ages-tome-of-secrets-discussion?p=999358#post999358\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I see that they have many behavioral variances, but nobody can deny the geniality of a Goratrix (one of my favorite characters in the WoD history, I mean, the guy makes the perfect villain) for instance. I also like Etrius, but he is very different from Goratrix, basically the other side of the coin, too cautious, too meticulous and with that strange &quot;holier than thou&quot; attitude that sounds even more strange when we're talking about usurpers lol. I see the Goratrix line as more lowly and &quot;two-faced&quot; or simply villainous and I'm not a big fan of Jervais, he's just too low! I also love the adventurous Celestyn, he's the kind of tremere everybody wants to be, but he's not a villain at all. But after all, the Tremere that conquered my heart was really Goratrix, the guy who came up with the potion of vampirism, that created the gargoyles, created a kind of artificial blood (although not very efficient lol) and ended up building his own house...oh and I can't forget that he made Tariq a 13th generation vampire, &quot;well deserved loser&quot; hahaha. I think I'd love to see WW develop more of his history, we need &quot;big bad guys&quot; like him. All in all, I like villains (I think almost every ST does lol) and I think the Tremere are great in this role.<br /> <br /> Cheers,<br /> Daniel.</div> </div> </div> </div>True. I think they're great in the role and they're a great tool. But this discussion has simply highlighted how much we already have of the Tremere. But how many Abyss Mystics or Koldun have we seen comparatively? Tremere in the past have gotten entire supplements all to themselves (House of Tremere and Blood Secrets of Thaumaturgy). Abyss Mysticism only existed in Guide to the High Clans in DA and didn't get more attention until the 20th Anniversary releases, the same with Koldunic Sorcery I think.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2818-frostfox","name":"FrostFox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2818_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"264"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-06T12:48:06-08:00","id":999378,"title":"","content":"Blood Magic dealt with Koldunic Sorcery and other kinds of sorcery as well as Thaumaturgy, it's basically a guide to blood sorcery. House Tremere is indeed only about Ceoris, the origin of the Tremere and some special chantries in the Dark Ages, like Etrius' Vienna Chantry, Goratrix's Paris Bastion and Meerlinda's Lion Gate. So the latter is basically a supplement for the Tremere, while the former is a general guide a little more focused on Hermetic Blood Sorcery, but also dealing with the others schools of blood magic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-06T13:21:05-08:00","id":999397,"title":"","content":"Alright: sell me the book.<br /> <br /> I thought DAV20 had some severe limitations.<br /> -Blood sorcery was thaumaturgy focused and incredibly limited on the basis that we were getting what the tremere had learnt so far (less than previous dark age books, Far less than you'd think with the logic of thaumaturgy being new. Like the Path of Conjuring's absence stuck out to me, as I'm pretty sure it should be around for settites and assamites at least at this point. Of particular note i'm currently playing a Baali who's avoided making deals with demons (and has promised herself she won't be messing around with that kind of stuff till she's at least a hundred and has the upper hand) whilst still practicing blood magic. (which one? We don't know. The proprietary wizardry of her sire I guess)<br /> -Absolutely nothing about sociology (which has been mentioned, and excites me) , a few bits of history/mythology equally revisionist to factual (or maybe it was mostly good, but jarring errors cause problems)<br /> -The &quot;We played skyrim&quot; weapon list. Full of anachronisms (broadsword) Vague terms (broadsword) and the obviously wrong (Warhammers doing 'blunt' damage)<br /> - A lack of information on nightlife. I tried to look it up. Seems like everyone just stays inside during the dark hours,for the next few hundred years, excepting maybe a few holidays. Which I guess means that Sneak-And-Drink is the universal way of the vampire. If that's absolutely correct, that's fine, but if it's not, we've got a huge slab of -missing- in how we can make nights more fun.<br /> -Also. vizier Quietus was basically a bad blood magic, plus a load of other clan/power changes that were good/bad/ugly. I guess there's also the issue of... Where's the conflict? I came here for issues, for struggles, for the great Jihad. DAV20 lacked any sort of thing for me to get angry about. If I hadn't read other vampire books, I guess this one'd be about mild politicking. <br /> <br /> <br /> So. Sociology. Blood magic. Tell me more.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Signatures are for terrible people who want to be caught.","edited":{"userid":12414,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12414-flower-innocent","user":"Flower,Innocent","date":". 11-06-2016, 04:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12414-flower-innocent","name":"Flower,Innocent","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12414_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"268"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-06T21:54:42-08:00","id":999575,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flower,Innocent</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/998155-v20-dark-ages-tome-of-secrets-discussion?p=999397#post999397\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Alright: sell me the book.<br /> The &quot;We played skyrim&quot; weapon list. Full of anachronisms (broadsword) Vague terms (broadsword) and the obviously wrong (Warhammers doing 'blunt' damage)</div> </div> </div> </div>Something is coming that will address this. To be fair though, we have a paradox: If the game used the correct terms, they would be confusing because most people are in fact familiar with the stereotypical weapons. For instance, you have to explain that a &quot;longsword&quot; is a two handed weapon, a &quot;broadsword&quot; is an 18th century weapon, a pick and a warhammer are usually two sides of the same thing, and the &quot;hammer&quot; is a collection of semi-sharp wedges.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Writer, Game Designer, Pro since 99.<br /> <br /> Thoughts at <a href=\"http://mobunited.com\" target=\"_blank\">mobunited.com</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/164-malcolm","name":"Malcolm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar164_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-06T22:39:30-08:00","id":999580,"title":"","content":"Not really.<br /> <br /> Sword. +2L<br /> Longsword. +3L<br /> Greatsword +4L<br /> <br /> They're nuetral terms. A sword could refer to an arming sword, a Talwar, Spartha, Wakazashi. Whatever.<br /> A greatsword is something really big that you need two hands for. A Claymore. A Zweihander. Odachi.<br /> A Longsword, by context of being between the two, is a -could use two hands- weapon. A Longsword, A Katana.<br /> <br /> That's all you need. You can put specific types of swords in italics under each item for examples, like VTM does with guns. You don't need to explain shit. If someone's curious, they'll look at the internet and research it themselves.<br /> <br /> (also note. Broadsword is confusingly both the 18th century basket hilt sword and the earlier scottish claymore, which'd be a greatsword. )<br /> <br /> A normal claw hammer that you'd get in a hardware store would do lethal, either end. A warhammer, designed to hurt people, would therefore be more lethal, no? Even if it's not a blade, It's a great deal of impact on a small point.<br /> Vampire uses real world history as part of it's setting. When we say 'warhammer'. We don't mean 'Giant Maul'. We mean a hammer. For war.<br /> Slings, similarly, are lethal, depending on the ammunition. ellipsoid lead bullets are death.<br /> <br /> Vampire is not DnD. We don't do 'resistance to slashing' 'double damage to bludgeoning'. 'Immune to cold attacks'. We have bashing, lethal, aggravated.So Why would anyone want a warhammer that does bashing when you could have a weapon that does the same with lethal? We've arbitrarily decided that some weapons are bashing, just to give their victims a brake. Did we pick up a warhammer because today we thought we'd incapacitate our enemies rather than murder them?<br /> <br /> Just being pedantic- DAV20 is set in the 1200's. Nobody uses two handed weapons right now (other than maybe spears and ranged weapons) because the main line of defense is the shield. In the future, armour will improve to the point of making the shield less relevant (which isn't reflected in stats. &quot;knight armour&quot; is just more dice) and everyone starts needing two handed weapons because<br /> -armour is now great and needs more power to get through<br /> -You don't need a shield anymore. Your armour is awesome.<br /> Now of course, maybe poor folk might still use shields since they can't get armour (Though they do need to compete more for a weapon)<br /> I get why future stuff is included (Plate armour comes in about 14th century, gets good in the 15th) but pointing it out woulda been good.<br /> <br /> Also. Ranged weapons. 4 armour piercing for longbows. What? +1 difficulty to throw a rock but nothing for dagger? As for melee/brawl. Where's all the stuff for dealing with tough folk quickly? I tried to run a solo game for a player, who's lamia got in a fight with two mooks. It lasted many rounds. They weren't wearing armour. I can't imagine if one was.<br /> (if good armour wasn't -3 dex, that'd be good too. Please balance things for mortals. Few can afford a 3 dex hit. Giving folk olympian dex to cope with plate isn't a good answer)<br /> <br /> This is totaly the wrong thread for this, But I've written everything anyway so I might as well post? I don't know: we didn't bother with a good weapon table, please buy another book for one? That kinda attitude is horrid.<br /> The writers didn't have a paradox. They just did the wrong thing. Gave it to Joe and told him 'Five minutes' or something like that.<br /> <i>(if there is a guy called Joe on the team. Sorry, That wasn't targeted) </i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Signatures are for terrible people who want to be caught.","edited":{"userid":12414,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12414-flower-innocent","user":"Flower,Innocent","date":". 11-07-2016, 01:57 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12414-flower-innocent","name":"Flower,Innocent","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12414_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"268"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-07T01:52:42-08:00","id":999623,"title":"","content":"What I am saying is that generations of tabletop and computer RPGs have defined the longsword as a one-handed weapon and the broadsword as a big-ish slashing/cutting weapon, so in terms of communicating what a weapon is, this is somewhat more accessible. That said, many of us are well aware of the difference between a hurlbat and a wimple full of rocks (the latter of which is a historically attested weapon for man/woman judicial combat),<br /> <br /> Now to address some of the other things you've said:<br /> <br /> * If Vampire had a realistic combat system, armour would be far too powerful. I do full contact armoured fighting with blunt steel. Mail over a gambeson wards off pretty much everything that isn't a thrust, and our mail isn't as good as historical examples. A strong cut might knock a few rings out. The course of evolution is really more of a matter of tradeoffs than armour suddenly becoming Super Next Level Shit. This is a complicated topic generally, not a simple Just So Story.<br /> * Actually, we do in fact play with damage this way. Vampires halve bashing damage after soak. The average mortal has a trivial ability to shrug off non-penetrating injuries but still get Incapacitated at short notice. &quot;Bashing&quot; is not &quot;bruising.&quot; It's simply blunt trauma (and possibly, superficial lacerations) of any severity.<br /> * Nah, there are two-handed swords from this period (XIIa and XIIIa on Oakeshott typology) though they're prevalent in the latter half of the century. They're just not especially distinct from their predecessors except for size and length.<br /> * Nah, an armed populace was common during the period -- in England you had to be armed if you had a certain amount of money.<br /> * People will argue about how well arrows penetrate armour until the end of time. I admit, rock vs. dagger is a concession to genre, but I will also submit that the rules don't live or die on this.<br /> * Why yes, clubbing people with your fists may require multiple intervals of three seconds if they're tough. The rules for mooks are on p. 351 of V20 Dark Ages. Mooks are not tough -- this is what makes them mooks. Now if you mean a high Stamina? Yes, mooks will take more time. If you don't want it to be a major fight, why would you give them high Stamina?<br /> <br /> I mean, let's work this out. Average mooks who know how to have dice pools of 4 and 4 HLs. They soak with 2 dice. Let's make the vampire a bit peppier, with 6 dice, 3 Sta soak and of course, all the HL's. Now if nobody defends themselves (which is pretty common for folks just throwing haymakers, and the vampire is tough) Assuming diff 6 across the board, every turn, the mooks score an average of 2 bashing. The vampire soaks one or two of these, and if one gets through, halves that last level, and suffers no damage. The vampire contemptuously beats up one, then the other, scoring an average of 3 damage, which the mooks soak an average of 1 of, so it takes four turns -- 12 seconds -- for a capable vampire to just beat the shit out of two mooks, with the vampire in all likelihood never getting hurt. If you designed mooks with higher Stamina and wanted them to get beaten quickly . . . well, you were preparing something at cross purposes with your goals. If you wanted a less capable vampire to win, well, vampire should've boosted some Physical Attributes. While Vampire's combat system isn't exactly peppy (major revisions to it are not in the mission of the 20th lines), it does't take ages to beat a mook -- and this is without me asking why this Lamia doesn't have any Potence. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Writer, Game Designer, Pro since 99.<br /> <br /> Thoughts at <a href=\"http://mobunited.com\" target=\"_blank\">mobunited.com</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/164-malcolm","name":"Malcolm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar164_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-07T01:56:18-08:00","id":999624,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flower,Innocent</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/998155-v20-dark-ages-tome-of-secrets-discussion?p=999397#post999397\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A lack of information on nightlife. I tried to look it up. Seems like everyone just stays inside during the dark hours,for the next few hundred years, excepting maybe a few holidays. Which I guess means that Sneak-And-Drink is the universal way of the vampire. If that's absolutely correct, that's fine, but if it's not, we've got a huge slab of -missing- in how we can make nights more fun.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fortunately for the purposes of the game, night-time in the medieval world was more interesting and active than that. Unfortunately, no-one has ever actually written a guide to the night-time world for <i>Vampire: the Dark Ages</i>, so the average player or Storyteller is left entirely in the dark (pun intended). This is, of course, one of the reasons why the texts of historical games actually have to include some history; the past can be so alien to the modern observer that it is hard to imagine how it was experienced without some guidance being available.<br /> <br /> (As it happens, the experience of night in the medieval world is probably the one thing I would write for Vampire: the Dark Ages if I had the opportunity, but, alas, it seems to be the kind of subject that is perpetually ignored.)<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/317-james_willoughby","name":"James_Willoughby","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar317_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-07T02:28:18-08:00","id":999631,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malcolm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/998155-v20-dark-ages-tome-of-secrets-discussion?p=999623#post999623\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Bunch of stuff I was going to say.</div> </div> </div> </div>What Malcolm said. <br /> <br /> And there was no Joe on the team. I wrote the weapons bit. And mostly, it was just a matter of redoing the old material. There were some things I was super passionate about revising. The weapons chart was not one of them. I listened to hundreds of comments about the old books. I never remember hearing anything about that material in the old books. So, I didn't want to invest a bunch of time in things nobody seemed particularly interested in getting a ton of attention. <br /> <br /> Likewise, I've never had your experiences with the combat system. I tend to find that there are more dice rolls than my players like, and multiple actions get boring for most of the table. But I've never seen a fight drag on, particularly when using the bit player rules on 351 that Malcolm mentions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-07T02:29:26-08:00","id":999633,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>James_Willoughby</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/998155-v20-dark-ages-tome-of-secrets-discussion?p=999624#post999624\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Fortunately for the purposes of the game, night-time in the medieval world was more interesting and active than that. Unfortunately, no-one has ever actually written a guide to the night-time world for <i>Vampire: the Dark Ages</i>, so the average player or Storyteller is left entirely in the dark (pun intended). This is, of course, one of the reasons why the texts of historical games actually have to include some history; the past can be so alien to the modern observer that it is hard to imagine how it was experienced without some guidance being available.<br /> <br /> (As it happens, the experience of night in the medieval world is probably the one thing I would write for Vampire: the Dark Ages if I had the opportunity, but, alas, it seems to be the kind of subject that is perpetually ignored.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Would you recommend any specific reading on the topic?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-07T05:22:22-08:00","id":999673,"title":"","content":".<br /> <br /> &quot;Bashing damage is blunt trauma humans heal rapidly. Lethal damage is serious tissue damage, lacerations, and other wounds that would leave a human to bleed out&quot;<br /> Getting hit by a warhammer. No doubt the second.<br /> <br /> *People specifically developed fighting techniques and such to deal with people in armour. I suspect they won't be used practically so much in HEMA, since getting around people's armour full force is generally a dick move that'll put you in a ward. Armour is supposed to be good. A cainite should react to a fellow strolling up with plate as they would someone weilding an assault shotgun. How else can you put the fear of men into mortals, baring hoping that they don't improvise throwing something should someone with true faith pop in.<br /> *yes. I'm entirely aware that we play with damage this way. That's why I'm pointing out how stupid it is to have a weapon designed to kill suddenly become some kind of two handed punch with reach. Why would anyone use a warhammer? &quot;Well dave, We were going against ghouls who soak lethal just like bashing so I thought it wouldn't matter if I used the hammer. Sorry something else came by and my weapon became entirely useless'<br /> *two handed swords existing during this time is a useless anecdote and you know it.<br /> <br /> <br /> As for that combat:<br /> The player was wearing armour. Class 4. She had potence 1 and fortitude 1 I think, but good inate physical stats. . She had a longsword and a spear. They used swords and had 4-5 dice. They had 4 health levels and heavy clothing.<br /> The +1 to all difficulties rule per extra greatly lengthened things. After that fight, I ruled that the character could disregard her own safety and reverse that rule into a -1 difficulty for opponents to hit, just to speed stuff along. We also looked greatly at rules like sweep and tackle to see if any down/murder combinations would work. Not without a second character or celerity it seems.<br /> <br /> <br /> Edit: Seems like you were the 'Joe'. Man. Not cool.<br /> &quot;I didn't want to put effort into this because I wasn't personally interested. Other things were interesting&quot;.<br /> I think you'll forgive me if I suggest this is lax.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Signatures are for terrible people who want to be caught.","edited":{"userid":12414,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12414-flower-innocent","user":"Flower,Innocent","date":". 11-07-2016, 08:24 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12414-flower-innocent","name":"Flower,Innocent","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12414_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"268"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-07T05:35:16-08:00","id":999678,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stannis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/998155-v20-dark-ages-tome-of-secrets-discussion?p=999235#post999235\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">i disagree man. the tremere are still unique. they're not just the thaumaturgy clan -</div> </div> </div> </div>But opposed to the other blood magic traditions they are somehow lacking really unique Tremere Path. With the exception of some really obscure (and often not really usefull) path, all of there path are shared with other traditions. These exclusive path are not really specific Tremere Path, it are just path the writers of the other traditions didn't put on the &quot;my tardition also knows these path&quot; list.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5199-aahz","name":"Aahz","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"610"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-07T05:47:15-08:00","id":999688,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flower,Innocent</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/998155-v20-dark-ages-tome-of-secrets-discussion?p=999673#post999673\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">.<br /> <br /> &amp;quot;Bashing damage is blunt trauma humans heal rapidly. Lethal damage is serious tissue damage, lacerations, and other wounds that would leave a human to bleed out&amp;quot;<br /> Getting hit by a warhammer. No doubt the second.<br /> <br /> *People specifically developed fighting techniques and such to deal with people in armour. I suspect they won't be used practically so much in HEMA, since getting around people's armour full force is generally a dick move that'll put you in a ward. Armour is supposed to be good. A cainite should react to a fellow strolling up with plate as they would someone weilding an assault shotgun. How else can you put the fear of men into mortals, baring hoping that they don't improvise throwing something should someone with true faith pop in.<br /> *yes. I'm entirely aware that we play with damage this way. That's why I'm pointing out how stupid it is to have a weapon designed to kill suddenly become some kind of two handed punch with reach. Why would anyone use a warhammer? &amp;quot;Well dave, We were going against ghouls who soak lethal just like bashing so I thought it wouldn't matter if I used the hammer. Sorry something else came by and my weapon became entirely useless'<br /> *two handed swords existing during this time is a useless anecdote and you know it.<br /> <br /> <br /> As for that combat:<br /> The player was wearing armour. Class 4. She had potence 1 and fortitude 1 I think, but good inate physical stats. . She had a longsword and a spear. They used swords and had 4-5 dice. They had 4 health levels and heavy clothing.<br /> The +1 to all difficulties rule per extra greatly lengthened things. After that fight, I ruled that the character could disregard her own safety and reverse that rule into a -1 difficulty for opponents to hit, just to speed stuff along. We also looked greatly at rules like sweep and tackle to see if any down/murder combinations would work. Not without a second character or celerity it seems.<br /> <br /> <br /> Edit: Seems like you were the 'Joe'. Man. Not cool.<br /> &amp;quot;I didn't want to put effort into this because I wasn't personally interested. Other things were interesting&amp;quot;.<br /> I think you'll forgive me if I suggest this is lax.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would say that the core book has the generic, accessible weapons chart most players expect and desire. To get more granular may confuse or irritate players looking for something quick and easy.<br /> <br /> Luckily for you, Dark Ages Companion goes into thorough detail on period appropriate weaponry and armour, so a hurrah for that!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#000080\">Matthew Dawkins</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000080\">In-House Developer for Onyx Path Publishing</span></b><br /> <br /> <i><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b><span style=\"color:#008080\">Website: </span><a href=\"http://www.matthewdawkins.com\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.matthewdawkins.com</span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#008080\">Patreon: </span><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins</span></a></b></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/152-the-gentleman-gamer","name":"The Gentleman Gamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar152_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-07T05:53:03-08:00","id":999690,"title":"","content":"Yeah, that's kind of what grinds my gears with Blood Magic today as well. The Tremere are supposed to be the foremost users of Thaumaturgy. Howerver, nowadays most of the independent clans as well as the Sabbat's two main clans have their own brand of it as well as the Anarchs.<br /> <br /> Sure, these practitioners are supposed to be rare compared to the Tremere, but every single one of these Thaumaturgists can do pretty much everything that the Tremere can AND MORE.<br /> <br /> If there are supposed to be so many forms of Thaumaturgy out there, at least give the Tremere some Paths and Rituals that the other don't have. Otherwise the Tremere will no longer be as interesting as they used to be.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imageshack.com/i/j5vvlqp\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/j5vvlqp\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/ghw20supporterhiddengaroup\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/n18segp\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0v25ewp\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">English is not my native language, so i apologize for errors in grammar or spelling.</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/392-cadmiumcadamium","name":"Cadmiumcadamium","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar392_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"936"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-07T06:20:48-08:00","id":999702,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flower,Innocent</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/998155-v20-dark-ages-tome-of-secrets-discussion?p=999673#post999673\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">.<br /> <br /> Edit: Seems like you were the 'Joe'. Man. Not cool.<br /> &quot;I didn't want to put effort into this because I wasn't personally interested. Other things were interesting&quot;.<br /> I think you'll forgive me if I suggest this is lax.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's not a quote. That's putting words into my mouth. And ones that grossly ignore what I actually said. I don't think you're engaging in good faith.<br /> <br /> It's a couple of pages out of a five hundred page book, where those couple of pages aren't the primary focus. I've talked to a ridiculous number of people about Dark Ages, and never heard any real complaints about that material. I didn't have any real complaints about it. So I didn't really change it much. I could point to a hundred things I likewise didn't change, because I didn't feel I needed to. And the changes from Revised to X20 really aren't significant enough to completely overhaul that base material.<br /> <br /> After over two years of work on the material, inordinate amounts of Open Development (where I heard no remarks in this regard) and a significant errata and revision pass (where I heard no remarks in this regard) I'm sorry you feel I didn't spend enough time on that specific content.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":70,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","user":"MachineIV","date":". 11-07-2016, 09:23 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-07T06:22:17-08:00","id":999704,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Gentleman Gamer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/998155-v20-dark-ages-tome-of-secrets-discussion?p=999688#post999688\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I would say that the core book has the generic, accessible weapons chart most players expect and desire. To get more granular may confuse or irritate players looking for something quick and easy.<br /> <br /> Luckily for you, Dark Ages Companion goes into thorough detail on period appropriate weaponry and armour, so a hurrah for that!</div> </div> </div> </div>I wasn't asking for something super precise. I don't care for the pros and cons of a hungarian longsword compared to a Tachi. And Getting the ins and outs of halfswording was never really more than a wishful thought. What I do care about, Is how w<i>rong</i> this weapon table gets. Broadswords, sabbers, bashing weapons, bows that fire armour piercing rounds. Oh my.<br /> <br /> It's not even balanced for gameplay. There's no incentive to use different weapons. There's a few good ones. A few crap ones. A few 'why would you ever use this' ones.<br /> <br /> Mage 20th goes into more detail. Heck: Vampire 20th goes into more detail (a few things, like flak jackets, are errenous), bit on the whole there's less mistakes.<br /> <br /> Edit: You didn't see anybody complain about it. But does that mean it's fixed?<br /> I don't know. I felt like maybe the culture had shifted and there were more historical nerds online now, playing RPGs. We see more realistic depictions of medieval society and warfare more often now. From historical series like vikings to even fantasies like game of thrones or even lord of the rings. Years ago, you expected big swords and conan outfits. I think people today are a little more able to sort out what's historical and what's an action movie taking artistic liscences. You can take a meander through youtube where people talk about swords, and go into interesting details about the design (This one works, this one works, this is silly but it works overall, you're joking, this one is excellent and I'd take it into a real battle) or analyse the choreography of a fight scene. It's a lot easier to get savvy nowadays (or at least pretend to be) and shouldn't vampire evolve with that? <br /> <br /> <br /> Cad:<br /> Old Skool, Dur-an-ki, Sadhanna, Akhu and whatever are far older than thaumaturgy. Yes, it is a shame that most of their unique stuff is garbage (wanna play with shadows?) and I do thing countermagic shouldn't be a thaumaturgy only thing.<br /> other magics are much smaller. Much more limited, and much more individual .A punk wanting a new spell is going to go through a lot more effort than a tremere to get it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Signatures are for terrible people who want to be caught.","edited":{"userid":12414,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12414-flower-innocent","user":"Flower,Innocent","date":". 11-07-2016, 09:35 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12414-flower-innocent","name":"Flower,Innocent","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12414_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"268"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-07T06:38:53-08:00","id":999713,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flower,Innocent</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/998155-v20-dark-ages-tome-of-secrets-discussion?p=999704#post999704\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">From historical series like vikings to even fantasies like game of thrones.</div> </div> </div> </div>Historian here. I could write you several articles about how inaccurate both of those shows are.<br /> <br /> Unless you're saying their combat is historically accurate. I don't know shit about military history and also I don't care very much, but you're over here conflating military history with the overall accuracy of a setting. That's bullshit. Every single medievalist I know goes on rants when they see people talking about Vikings and Game of Thrones. One professor I studied with in Gothenburg, Sweden particularly loved ranting about historical inaccuracies in the Vikings. This historian:<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://historiskastudier.gu.se/english/Staff/henrik-janson\" target=\"_blank\">http://historiskastudier.gu.se/engli.../henrik-janson</a><br /> <br /> He also took me around Old Norse burial sites and literally just translated tombstones in front of me. Like, leaned over sideways and translated them right there.<br /> <br /> If you want to criticize the text for lacking what you wanted insofar as useful combat material, that's one thing. Do whatever the hell you want there. I can't tell you if it's accurate or not. I can tell you that feudalism and chivalry are both modern constructs. I can tell you about family and town structure in medieval Europe. I can tell you about medicine and medical practices. I can do all that as an historian who's technically not a medievalist. Don't say Vikings and Game of Thrones are historically accurate if what you mean is &quot;they get combat right to my specifications&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:12px\">-</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3093-hm8453a","name":"hm8453a","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3093_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"636"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-07T07:29:15-08:00","id":999731,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flower,Innocent</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/998155-v20-dark-ages-tome-of-secrets-discussion?p=999704#post999704\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Cad:<br /> Old Skool, Dur-an-ki, Sadhanna, Akhu and whatever are far older than thaumaturgy. Yes, it is a shame that most of their unique stuff is garbage (wanna play with shadows?) and I do thing countermagic shouldn't be a thaumaturgy only thing.<br /> other magics are much smaller. Much more limited, and much more individual .A punk wanting a new spell is going to go through a lot more effort than a tremere to get it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm fully aware that a lot of the various forms of Blood Magic are older than Hermetic Thaumaturgy used by the Tremere. It just pisses me off that a lot of the really cool things that Tremere were (in)famous for in 2nd edition just got relegated to &quot;oh, well every blood mage has access to that now&quot;.<br /> For the longest time i was adamant that Path of Blood was Tremere specific until a good friend of mine made me realize that it didn't really make sense (i still think it should be Tremere specific but can see others points of view).<br /> <br /> I would however like to see a series of Paths and Rituals based on Hermetic theories (stripped of the trappings and foci of their forebearers) that are Tremere specific, that no one else has access to.<br /> <br /> \u200bI have no problem with Lure of Flames, MotM, Path of Conjuring etc being available to basically every form of Blood Magic but to me Path of Blood is quintessentially Tremere magic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imageshack.com/i/j5vvlqp\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/j5vvlqp\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/ghw20supporterhiddengaroup\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/n18segp\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0v25ewp\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">English is not my native language, so i apologize for errors in grammar or spelling.</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/392-cadmiumcadamium","name":"Cadmiumcadamium","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar392_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"936"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-07T07:39:10-08:00","id":999734,"title":"","content":"A note on Warhammers, from a historical perspective.<br /> <br /> They were originally designed as a counter-weapon to medieval armors, with the purpose to deal extreme concussive damage that didn't need to penetrate the armor to deal effective focused damage, while at the same time of course being quite deadly to non-armored enemies. Originally they had no spike, only the hammer part, and usually had a long shaft for effective swings, and in some regards could be considered pole weapons, especially the models used against mounted opponents that were almost halberd-size sometimes. Spikes were quickly added however to this effective weapon to make it even more versatile and deadly.<br /> <br /> Most fantasy setting games (DnD we're looking at you) always got the Warhammer-part confused with Mauls, a weapon that didn't appear until 14th century or so. So that's that. Ironically old school rpg's like Rolemaster actually got the Warhammer defined more correctly as more of a spike weapon than a club weapon. But the rpg legacy has Warhammers all confused, usually calling what actually is a regular Warhammer for War Mattock instead.<br /> <br /> When inconcistencies like this appear in rpg books, I correct them myself. It's not hard to do. Especially not in a storytellign setting where everything is supposed to be more of guidelines in how to create dramatic conflict and scenery and not tactically correct combat. For that I recommend stuff like Phoenix Command. Hahaha. Have fun with that. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/deluxe-hunters-hunted-ii\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img692/7017/hh2support.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><a href=\"https://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/deluxe-anarchs-unbound\" target=\"_blank\"> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img703/6636/6kvo.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> <a href=\"https://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/deluxe-mage-the-ascension-20th-anniversary-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img31/2512/25ew.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> <a href=\"https://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/deluxe-w20-book-of-the-wyrm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/507-ignytezero","name":"IgnyteZero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar507_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-07T07:46:05-08:00","id":999738,"title":"","content":"They're not historically accurate. They're better than world of warcraft or Blade II. In video games we're getting more things like mount and blade, kindom come, war of the roses. Yes. They're not fighting realistically, and I too could give plenty of gripes about vikings or thrones like how every lanister pleb is wearing plate or how vikings aren't using colourful dyes. But the point is they're <i>better</i>. They're not running around with oversized swords slung to their backs. They're not pretending the spear doesn't exist. They're moving away from trying to hit eachother's sword (even though the occasional lapse comes in)<br /> <br /> It's not accurate. But it's <i>better</i>. And here we are in a setting that's set in actual history, and we're confusing mauls with warhammers again.<br /> <br /> IgnyteZero stealing my thunder.<br /> I too correct stuff. But it's a thing you need to communicate well with players. I do a lot of houserules for ballance/logistical concerns/ more in depth combat. <br /> But I shouldn't have to rebalance so much. In mage, i'd just hunt down the Greatswords and the difficulty 4 daggers and call it a day. Here, most things are in the wrong.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Signatures are for terrible people who want to be caught.","edited":{"userid":12414,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12414-flower-innocent","user":"Flower,Innocent","date":". 11-07-2016, 10:53 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12414-flower-innocent","name":"Flower,Innocent","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12414_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"268"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-07T07:54:34-08:00","id":999739,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cadmiumcadamium</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/998155-v20-dark-ages-tome-of-secrets-discussion?p=999731#post999731\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">other magics are much smaller. Much more limited, and much more individual .A punk wanting a new spell is going to go through a lot more effort than a tremere to get it.</div> </div> </div> </div>But as a SC you will anyway be kind of limited in the amount of powers you can learn and have to cherry pick the good ones. And Punks and other Anarch Sorcerers might be rare, but they are iirc more willing to share their secrets and require probbaly less payment.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5199-aahz","name":"Aahz","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"610"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-07T07:57:08-08:00","id":999741,"title":"","content":"<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flower,Innocent</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/998155-v20-dark-ages-tome-of-secrets-discussion?p=999738#post999738\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They're not historically accurate. They're better than world of warcraft or Blade II. In video games we're getting more things like mount and blade, kindom come, war of the roses. Yes. They're not fighting realistically, and I too could give plenty of gripes about vikings or thrones like how every lanister pleb is wearing plate or how vikings aren't using colourful dyes. But the point is they're <i>better</i>. They're not running around with oversized swords slung to their backs. They're not pretending the spear doesn't exist. They're moving away from trying to hit eachother's sword (even though the occasional lapse comes in)<br /> <br /> It's not accurate. But it's <i>better</i>. And here we are in a setting that's set in actual history, and we're confusing mauls with warhammers again.</div> </div> </div> </div>Then play a wargame. Don't come here and revise your statement after you're called out. You said they're historically accurate, after essentializing historical accuracy as doing combat the way you would. I told you they weren't historically accurate at all, and then you said you'd never said they were. Stand by your words. If you're saying they're historically accurate insofar as military history, again, I can't argue with that. I've said I can't. I truly do not know, and I'm not interested enough to find out. But that's not what you said. Here's what you said:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flower,Innocent</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/998155-v20-dark-ages-tome-of-secrets-discussion?p=999704#post999704\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I felt like maybe the culture had shifted and there were more historical nerds online now, playing RPGs. We see more <b>realistic depictions of medieval society</b> and warfare more often now. From historical series like vikings to even fantasies like game of thrones or even lord of the rings. Years ago, you expected big swords and conan [sic] outfits. I think people today are a little more able to sort out what's historical and what's an action movie taking artistic liscences [sic] [bold mine].</div> </div> </div> </div>Historical. That is the word you used. &quot;Realistic depictions of medieval society and warfare.&quot; &quot;Sort out what's historical&quot;. Neither Vikings nor Game of Thrones is historical. Neither Vikings nor Game of Thrones hosts realistic depictions of medieval society. Again, I freely admit I cannot comment on warfare.<br /> <br /> There are plenty of things I wish were in every single OPP text that aren't. But we--and the other writers--can't read your mind, and we can't please everyone. The book could be twelve thousand pages, and then we'd get more complaints about time and release. From what David has said--and it sounds pretty easily verifiable--you did not say during open development that you were unhappy because you wanted more weapons stats in a game that's not about combat. If you had said that, maybe we could have incorporated it, or maybe not. Maybe David still would have decided it wasn't worth having to hire another writer for something that one person wants. We can all brainstorm and get these stats organized here, for you and anyone else who would like them, but it's ridiculous to assert that there's a major fault in the text because the writers couldn't read your mind and give you exactly what you wanted when you didn't say you wanted it, and when it wasn't the purpose of the book to begin with.\u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:12px\">-</span>","edited":{"userid":3093,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3093-hm8453a","user":"hm8453a","date":". 11-07-2016, 11:00 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3093-hm8453a","name":"hm8453a","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3093_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"636"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-07T08:09:25-08:00","id":999750,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cadmiumcadamium</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/998155-v20-dark-ages-tome-of-secrets-discussion?p=999731#post999731\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm fully aware that a lot of the various forms of Blood Magic are older than Hermetic Thaumaturgy used by the Tremere. It just pisses me off that a lot of the really cool things that Tremere were (in)famous for in 2nd edition just got relegated to &quot;oh, well every blood mage has access to that now&quot;.<br /> For the longest time i was adamant that Path of Blood was Tremere specific until a good friend of mine made me realize that it didn't really make sense (i still think it should be Tremere specific but can see others points of view).<br /> <br /> I would however like to see a series of Paths and Rituals based on Hermetic theories (stripped of the trappings and foci of their forebearers) that are Tremere specific, that no one else has access to.<br /> <br /> \u200bI have no problem with Lure of Flames, MotM, Path of Conjuring etc being available to basically every form of Blood Magic but to me Path of Blood is quintessentially Tremere magic.</div> </div> </div> </div>Interesting point: I run Tremere that way. I make the Path of Blood their exclusive practice, and most Thaumaturgic rituals the same. I see Hermetic magic more in the rituals of the Discipline than the paths.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#000080\">Matthew Dawkins</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000080\">In-House Developer for Onyx Path Publishing</span></b><br /> <br /> <i><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b><span style=\"color:#008080\">Website: </span><a href=\"http://www.matthewdawkins.com\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.matthewdawkins.com</span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#008080\">Patreon: </span><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins</span></a></b></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/152-the-gentleman-gamer","name":"The Gentleman Gamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar152_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-07T08:30:52-08:00","id":999761,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hm8453a</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/998155-v20-dark-ages-tome-of-secrets-discussion?p=999741#post999741\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> Then play a wargame. Don't come here and revise your statement after you're called out. .\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>You strawman a lot. I understand you're emotive because someone's attacking your work specifically, but A revised statement doesn't invalidate the statement. This isn't something one person wanted. I remember going into discussion with half the coterie about it. I wasn't participating in any of the open development stuff (was the weapon table a thing? I remember picking up a WiP and didn't see it.) , but You shouldn't need to be asked to do the right thing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Signatures are for terrible people who want to be caught.","edited":{"userid":12414,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12414-flower-innocent","user":"Flower,Innocent","date":". 11-07-2016, 11:32 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12414-flower-innocent","name":"Flower,Innocent","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12414_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"268"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-07T08:34:51-08:00","id":999766,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flower,Innocent</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/998155-v20-dark-ages-tome-of-secrets-discussion?p=999761#post999761\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I understand you're emotive.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yawn. Stopped reading, and I'm done engaging with you.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:12px\">-</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3093-hm8453a","name":"hm8453a","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3093_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"636"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-07T09:20:25-08:00","id":999783,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hm8453a</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/998155-v20-dark-ages-tome-of-secrets-discussion?p=999766#post999766\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yawn. Stopped reading, and I'm done engaging with you.</div> </div> </div> </div>How constructive. Could you back out in a way that makes it any less apparent that your arguments fall short? <br /> I dunno. Maybe I have a right to be concerned when the 'historian' writing the piece states &quot;I don't care very much&quot; and he did it the way it's always done. You'd think the person who calls themself a historian would go for accuracy, right? <br /> <br /> Vampire is about warfare. The struggle. The Jyhad. It's a social game, but it's also a physical one. But thematically, Vampire isn't about champions. Your heroes are conflicted dicks in a shit world. The world of darkness is shades of grey with shades of black, and anything white is an enemy or going to be snuffed out. <br /> <br /> History aside, It doesn't thematically fit to have high fantasy tropes in vampire. You're not four mixed race, different classed characters charging up the mountain to defeat the dread necromancer who's been plaguing the village they want to save. It's more likely that you're four conflicted and angry fellows who're hoping to diablerize the tzmisce lord and claim his occult resources. You'll later kill eachother over how to divide his domain, and the lord's practice of making sport of the locals might be something you'll pick up, but because you didn't care for them anyway, not because the tzmisce you ate is now a part of you. <br /> These aren't the sort of stories that fit the colourful RPGs we usually get. Huge pauldrons, giant weapons and skimpy female armours aren't what we're looking for. It's the gritty, realist stuff. Yes, vampire can get outlandish at times (the vampire-necromancer- goth girl with a holy claymore developed over time in a game of mine) but that just points at the varied range that vampires draw from. Vampire was never supposed tobe about heroic quests, which is what DAV20's incorrect, fantasy inspired weapons table implies.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Signatures are for terrible people who want to be caught.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12414-flower-innocent","name":"Flower,Innocent","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12414_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"268"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-07T11:50:26-08:00","id":999845,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> How constructive. Could you back out in a way that makes it any less apparent that your arguments fall short? </div> </div> </div>It seems extremely fair to stop engaging in a conversation when someone starts making insulting comments, implying a lot of disingenuity several times on the writers' part, and revising their statements.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12552-monalfie","name":"Monalfie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12552_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-07T11:55:25-08:00","id":999847,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flower,Innocent</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/998155-v20-dark-ages-tome-of-secrets-discussion?p=999673#post999673\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">.<br /> &quot;Bashing damage is blunt trauma humans heal rapidly. Lethal damage is serious tissue damage, lacerations, and other wounds that would leave a human to bleed out&quot;<br /> Getting hit by a warhammer. No doubt the second.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not really. Even those four wedges (which are about an inch long) are not deep penetrators the way a dagger is, and do not create deep cuts the way a swords does. You're right in that the &quot;warhammer&quot; really is a maul by the rules. If I swung a maul at your chest, you would fall down. If I swung a pick at your chest, you would have a spike in an organ.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> *People specifically developed fighting techniques and such to deal with people in armour. I suspect they won't be used practically so much in HEMA, since getting around people's armour full force is generally a dick move that'll put you in a ward. </div> </div> </div>I am well aware of how half-swording and murderstrokes work. Plate armor doesn't make you immune to them, and my point is that plate is not quite an enormous leap in protection, except perhaps against thrusts.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Armour is supposed to be good. A cainite should react to a fellow strolling up with plate as they would someone weilding an assault shotgun. How else can you put the fear of men into mortals, baring hoping that they don't improvise throwing something should someone with true faith pop in. </div> </div> </div>It works well enough. Keep in mind that mortals normally have *no soak* versus lethal damage. None. This means that yes, vampires walk around as if armoured all the time. This makes them frightening.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> *yes. I'm entirely aware that we play with damage this way. That's why I'm pointing out how stupid it is to have a weapon designed to kill suddenly become some kind of two handed punch with reach. Why would anyone use a warhammer? &quot;Well dave, We were going against ghouls who soak lethal just like bashing so I thought it wouldn't matter if I used the hammer. Sorry something else came by and my weapon became entirely useless' </div> </div> </div>Mortals don't devise weapons assuming they'll fight ghouls with them. I will grant you that maces and such should penetrate armour better.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> *two handed swords existing during this time is a useless anecdote and you know it. </div> </div> </div>This is a misconception created by the fact that early two handed swords are classified as subtypes due to having the same blade geometry regardless of length.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> As for that combat:<br /> The player was wearing armour. Class 4. She had potence 1 and fortitude 1 I think, but good inate physical stats. . She had a longsword and a spear. They used swords and had 4-5 dice. They had 4 health levels and heavy clothing.<br /> The +1 to all difficulties rule per extra greatly lengthened things. After that fight, I ruled that the character could disregard her own safety and reverse that rule into a -1 difficulty for opponents to hit, just to speed stuff along. We also looked greatly at rules like sweep and tackle to see if any down/murder combinations would work. Not without a second character or celerity it seems. </div> </div> </div>So this isn't a simple brawl, but an attempt to defeat two people in light armour with swords. I have no idea where the +1 difficulty is coming from besides engaging multiple opponents. So:<br /> <br /> Vampire: Dice pool 4(6-2), 7 HL, 8 soak (Sta 3 + armour and Fortitude 1), Dam 5+1 Fortitude (Str 3 + 2).<br /> * Vampire scores 2 successes to strike on average, and inflicts 3.5 damage, +1 for Potence for 4.5, assuming the vampire spends 1 blood point.<br /> * Vampire soaks an average of 4 damage.<br /> <br /> Dudes: Dice pool 4, 4 HL, 1 soak. Dam 4 (Str 2 +2).<br /> * Dudes score 2 successes to strike on average, and inflict 3 damage.<br /> * Dudes soak .5 damage, on average.<br /> <br /> What do we end up with? The same scenario. An armored vampire with Fortitude suffers little to no damage, and may well kill one opponent per turn. The vampire can once again opt not to defend herself. Now things will swing one way or the other, which is why we have things like blood point and Willpower expenditures. And of course the vampire'd dice pool would be lower if attacking them both at the same time.<br /> <br /> But the fact is, if you want a vampire to waste multiple Extras per turn, you need to create a vampire who can waste multiple Extras per turn with some combination of Celerity or significant dice pools. Plus the goal posts, they are shifting. Your initial complaint is about lack of realism and armour being weak -- but you wanted this character to waste two sword-wielders like it was nothing and earlier, complain that armour would have made it take forever.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Edit: Seems like you were the 'Joe'. Man. Not cool.<br /> &quot;I didn't want to put effort into this because I wasn't personally interested. Other things were interesting&quot;.<br /> I think you'll forgive me if I suggest this is lax. </div> </div> </div>I didn't work on the core.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Writer, Game Designer, Pro since 99.<br /> <br /> Thoughts at <a href=\"http://mobunited.com\" target=\"_blank\">mobunited.com</a></b>","edited":{"userid":164,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/164-malcolm","user":"Malcolm","date":". 11-07-2016, 02:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/164-malcolm","name":"Malcolm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar164_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-07T12:09:26-08:00","id":999853,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flower,Innocent</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/998155-v20-dark-ages-tome-of-secrets-discussion?p=999783#post999783\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How constructive. Could you back out in a way that makes it any less apparent that your arguments fall short?<br /> I dunno. Maybe I have a right to be concerned when the 'historian' writing the piece states &quot;I don't care very much&quot; and he did it the way it's always done. You'd think the person who calls themself a historian would go for accuracy, right?<br /> <br /> Vampire is about warfare. The struggle. The Jyhad. It's a social game, but it's also a physical one. But thematically, Vampire isn't about champions. Your heroes are conflicted dicks in a shit world. The world of darkness is shades of grey with shades of black, and anything white is an enemy or going to be snuffed out.<br /> <br /> History aside, It doesn't thematically fit to have high fantasy tropes in vampire. You're not four mixed race, different classed characters charging up the mountain to defeat the dread necromancer who's been plaguing the village they want to save. It's more likely that you're four conflicted and angry fellows who're hoping to diablerize the tzmisce lord and claim his occult resources. You'll later kill eachother over how to divide his domain, and the lord's practice of making sport of the locals might be something you'll pick up, but because you didn't care for them anyway, not because the tzmisce you ate is now a part of you.<br /> These aren't the sort of stories that fit the colourful RPGs we usually get. Huge pauldrons, giant weapons and skimpy female armours aren't what we're looking for. It's the gritty, realist stuff. Yes, vampire can get outlandish at times (the vampire-necromancer- goth girl with a holy claymore developed over time in a game of mine) but that just points at the varied range that vampires draw from. Vampire was never supposed tobe about heroic quests, which is what DAV20's incorrect, fantasy inspired weapons table implies.</div> </div> </div> </div>Really a bit of a stretch to say a weapons table codifies an entire line of storytelling, eh?<br /> <br /> Anyway, DAV plays loose with history in a number of ways, mostly for the sake of providing story inspirations and to lay down Gothic storytelling motifs. Like, even your &quot;corrected&quot; story of going up to get the Tzimisce relies on that very tweaking, because there was a definite shortage of big scary castles in Eastern Europe during the period -- they come later, replacing somewhat more modest wooden forts. But we've got them anyway because they look cool. We have elder's labyrinths that are, indeed, full of hazards -- they're positively dungeonlike! And you can even recruit a glowing vampire paladin to help you out, if you want to reach back to 1e. But you can also play it without those elements.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Writer, Game Designer, Pro since 99.<br /> <br /> Thoughts at <a href=\"http://mobunited.com\" target=\"_blank\">mobunited.com</a></b>","edited":{"userid":164,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/164-malcolm","user":"Malcolm","date":". 11-07-2016, 03:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/164-malcolm","name":"Malcolm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar164_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-07T12:24:55-08:00","id":999872,"title":"","content":"I appreciate historical accuracy, to a degree, but I also want to play Vampire. I think it's fine to accept that some elements of reality will need to take a trip out the window.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#000080\">Matthew Dawkins</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000080\">In-House Developer for Onyx Path Publishing</span></b><br /> <br /> <i><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b><span style=\"color:#008080\">Website: </span><a href=\"http://www.matthewdawkins.com\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.matthewdawkins.com</span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#008080\">Patreon: </span><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins</span></a></b></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/152-the-gentleman-gamer","name":"The Gentleman Gamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar152_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-07T12:29:14-08:00","id":999879,"title":"","content":"I don't know where to begin.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flower,Innocent</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/998155-v20-dark-ages-tome-of-secrets-discussion?p=999761#post999761\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You strawman a lot. I understand you're emotive because someone's attacking your work specifically, but A revised statement doesn't invalidate the statement. This isn't something one person wanted. I remember going into discussion with half the coterie about it. I wasn't participating in any of the open development stuff (was the weapon table a thing? I remember picking up a WiP and didn't see it.) , but You shouldn't need to be asked to do the right thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>You can drop sexism left and right, but no, Hayley's not being emotive, she's being completely resoned and logical. How the hell can you accuse her of dropping strawmen? She's quoting you directly, and responding nearly line by line where it's relevant. Look in the mirror. She wrote out several extremely useful posts that would likely hep you if you'd pay attention.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flower,Innocent</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/998155-v20-dark-ages-tome-of-secrets-discussion?p=999783#post999783\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How constructive. Could you back out in a way that makes it any less apparent that your arguments fall short?<br /> I dunno. Maybe I have a right to be concerned when the 'historian' writing the piece states &quot;I don't care very much&quot; and he did it the way it's always done. You'd think the person who calls themself a historian would go for accuracy, right?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>And now I'm just confused as hell. Hayley didn't write the section you're angry about. David did. This has been established on the thread. Hayley is a historian. David is not. Hayley is not a military historian, she is an early Americanist. This has all been established. None of it had any bearing at all on whether or not you would get your precious table, because she didn't write the section. She also didn't decide who wrote what section. As for &quot;maybe I have a right to be concerned when the 'historian' writing the piece states &quot;I don't care very much&quot; and he did it the way it's always done,&quot; I'm just floored. I don't even understand what you're writing anymore. She didn't write it. She didn't do it the way it's always done, because she didn't do it at all. And she's not a &quot;he&quot;. At this point, I feel like you're not even reading the thread, because you seem to be confusing David Hill and Hayley Margules.<br /> <br /> Moreover, Hayley Margules doesn't owe you anything. Why should she stay when you're dropping sexist insults, not arguing in good faith, and don't even understand the facts of what's going on enough to know she and David are different people? Why should she give you anything at all?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>International Relations Scholar, Salesman, and GM. Guess which one of those is my favorite?","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12305-obrimosmaintenance","name":"ObrimosMaintenance","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-07T12:35:27-08:00","id":999884,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flower,Innocent</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/998155-v20-dark-ages-tome-of-secrets-discussion?p=999761#post999761\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You strawman a lot. I understand you're emotive because someone's attacking your work specifically, but A revised statement doesn't invalidate the statement. This isn't something one person wanted. I remember going into discussion with half the coterie about it. I wasn't participating in any of the open development stuff (was the weapon table a thing? I remember picking up a WiP and didn't see it.) , but You shouldn't need to be asked to do the right thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>1) Don't backhandedly accuse someone of being irrational. Deploy your own arguments respectfully.<br /> 2) A weapons table is not really a site upon which moral stakes are set.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Writer, Game Designer, Pro since 99.<br /> <br /> Thoughts at <a href=\"http://mobunited.com\" target=\"_blank\">mobunited.com</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":12}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/164-malcolm","name":"Malcolm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar164_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-07T12:43:37-08:00","id":999892,"title":"","content":"Let's move on from the discussion of weapons not even appearing in the book of which this thread is a focus. For future weaponry and combat rules, check out the V20 Dark Ages Companion when it comes out! There's some excellent content in there, written by our very own, extremely talented Malcolm Sheppard (above).<br /> <br /> On the subject of Tome of Secrets, let's draw things back to the positive. What do people enjoy from the book?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#000080\">Matthew Dawkins</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000080\">In-House Developer for Onyx Path Publishing</span></b><br /> <br /> <i><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b><span style=\"color:#008080\">Website: </span><a href=\"http://www.matthewdawkins.com\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.matthewdawkins.com</span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#008080\">Patreon: </span><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins</span></a></b></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/152-the-gentleman-gamer","name":"The Gentleman Gamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar152_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-07T12:54:07-08:00","id":999900,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Gentleman Gamer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/998155-v20-dark-ages-tome-of-secrets-discussion?p=999892#post999892\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On the subject of Tome of Secrets, let's draw things back to the positive. What do people enjoy from the book?</div> </div> </div> </div>The art is great and does an excellent job of capturing &quot;Vampire&quot; in my opinion. I'm particular fond the of the art on page 51(One with the forest) and the knight on page 8.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-07T14:15:28-08:00","id":999941,"title":"","content":"Yeah, gentleman, you're probably right.<br /> <br /> Is there anything on misc practices of blood magic? There's a massive gap of western european magic before the tremere and i was wondering if anything has tried to fill it? <br /> <br /> PS: Obrimons there was no sexism in anything I said. I was under no knowledge as to the gender of hm untill it was brought up in this thread, by you. Implications.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Signatures are for terrible people who want to be caught.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12414-flower-innocent","name":"Flower,Innocent","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12414_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"268"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-07T15:03:37-08:00","id":999963,"title":"","content":"It is known when the Tome's pdf will be avaible on Drivethru?<br /> I can't wait to have more details on Koldunism.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12142-undead-rabbit","name":"Undead rabbit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-07T16:39:21-08:00","id":1000017,"title":"","content":"I wasn't sure where this accusation of sexism came from either, but also not entirely sure why weapons charts are that big a deal.<br /> <br /> Anyway, I'm not really sure what I think about the book, so far. It kind of feels like how I felt about the Dark Ages 20th book in some ways. I really loved the style, the art, the visuals, but wasn't as sold on the writing. In this case, and this is completely subjective, I didn't really care for the vast majority of the magical sections dealing with Thaumaturgy styles. I don't know, I can't place my finger(s) on it, but it seemed like a large break from prior concepts and material for the sake of trying to push something new, but also comes off, at least on early reading as largely unplayable and unusable.<br /> <br /> Borderline like trying to get someone's own home game into published canon. But I'm not sure that's right, or to what extent, and there is certainly some degree of not liking change, especially as contradictions to, (or not knowing of), prior material. Some of it, like with the Koldun, I felt was a backwards step (and like I mentioned, gets very close to making it unusable), and I literally thought as I was reading it, &quot;someone is trying to make Sith Vampires&quot;. <br /> <br /> I think my biggest gripes are that I think this book really just wasn't for me. It seemed to overly focus on things I didn't really care much about and barely (if at all) touch on things I would love to see ten times more of, (Knightly Orders and Holy things come to mind).<br /> <br /> Despite my original reservations, I actually really liked the rules and thought put into the Knightly Fighting style/maneuvers, and I'd like to see more of this sort of thing all around, (doesn't need to be combat orientated). Little things that can help personalize characters.<br /> <br /> At the same time, considering that I got it for free, in a sense, I can't complain too much. I don't care for it much, or the direction that the Vampire 20th line seems to be heading, but, perhaps once I read it again and more that might change?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://t0.gstatic.com/images?q=tbn:ANd9GcTAO8runv-CR5dodCXgw_8wdJype5yunYCODWdZiBAwUP5WFVv8\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://ksr-ugc.imgix.net/assets/003/593/392/92a29c2836b988505781770a32720148_original.png?v=1428699067&amp;w=700&amp;h=&amp;fit=max&amp;auto=format&amp;lossless=true&amp;s=69ffdde357a0cdd88ee89934622443f9\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img692/7017/hh2support.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img703/6636/6kvo.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1721-beckett","name":"Beckett","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1721_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1077"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-07T16:58:38-08:00","id":1000023,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Gentleman Gamer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/998155-v20-dark-ages-tome-of-secrets-discussion?p=999872#post999872\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I appreciate historical accuracy, to a degree, but I also want to play Vampire. I think it's fine to accept that some elements of reality will need to take a trip out the window.</div> </div> </div> </div>And hasn't that always been stated about WoD, in all the game lines? That WoD is more of a dark dismal echo of our own reality.<br /> <br /> In the end it's all about suspension of disbelief though. To some an anachronistic weapontable destroys that, for others it is errors in descriptions of social structures in a certain culture or era. It's hard to get every detail right.<br /> <br /> Historians make a difference between Cultural Heritage and Actual History. Most of the history we know collectively is actually cultural heritage, not actual history. So I do think that even though we should expect the writers to be fairly correct in historical assumptions, they deserve some leeway. It is very easy to mix up history you thought was actual history with cultural heritage. Because you will make subconscious assumptions where it is blank.<br /> <br /> I assume that's what happened here. Sadly. But it's really no big deal.<br /> <br /> It would have been nice to see a more accurate weapon table, or even chapter. More like in the Revised ST companion but for DAV. But Tome of Secrets don't feel like it would have been the right place for that.<br /> <br /> But... Do you know what this means? There's still room for OP to make even more books for the game! There's still content we need <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> As for ToS itself I've only skimmed the pdf. I'm a traditionalist and prefer to lean back with my hardcover copy and take it all in. But some few words I can share is...<br /> <br /> 1. I dislike that it keeps following the tradition of the streamlined rules for Thaumaturgy found in DAV20 and Rites of Blood, because it ignores and/or simplifies a lot of great content without obvious purpose.<br /> <br /> 2. I lean towards really liking the Abyss and Koldun parts though. The Abyss stuff feels like a great tool for storytelling, so very useful for me as an ST even though PC's won't find much use for it most likely. But that's just as it should be as I see it. This is the Tome of Secrets, not the Tome of General Knowledge. And I don't mind the Sith-iness of Koldunism, since I find it works greatly with how I've used Tzimisce/Old Clan and Kolduns in my games. And it fits greatly with other V20 material on the subject imho. Also loved the Harbinger connection.<br /> <br /> 3. The knight and war stuff seems to work great, at least from my superficial understanding. Previous systems have been lacking to say the least so this could be very helpful.<br /> <br /> 4. More faith stuff? I am ambivalent here. Is it necessary? Maybe not. Does it help? Probably, considering how important religion was back then. So yeah, why not?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/deluxe-hunters-hunted-ii\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img692/7017/hh2support.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><a href=\"https://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/deluxe-anarchs-unbound\" target=\"_blank\"> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img703/6636/6kvo.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> <a href=\"https://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/deluxe-mage-the-ascension-20th-anniversary-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img31/2512/25ew.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> <a href=\"https://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/deluxe-w20-book-of-the-wyrm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a>","edited":{"userid":507,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/507-ignytezero","user":"IgnyteZero","date":". 11-09-2016, 07:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/507-ignytezero","name":"IgnyteZero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar507_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-07T22:42:01-08:00","id":1000156,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Gentleman Gamer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/998155-v20-dark-ages-tome-of-secrets-discussion?p=999750#post999750\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Interesting point: I run Tremere that way. I make the Path of Blood their exclusive practice, and most Thaumaturgic rituals the same. I see Hermetic magic more in the rituals of the Discipline than the paths.</div> </div> </div> </div>But according to the V20 rules, it is also a path used in Du-An-Ki, Wanga, Nahuallotl, New Age Blood Magic, Punk Sorcery and Hacktivist Thaumaturgy.<br /> <br /> If we ignore the Anarch Tarditions, the only Tremere paths that are not available for the other big traditions are The Green Path, Path of the Levinbolt and Path of Technomancy. (With the Anarchs they have no exclusive path left.)<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5199-aahz","name":"Aahz","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"610"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-08T01:24:10-08:00","id":1000181,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Beckett</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/998155-v20-dark-ages-tome-of-secrets-discussion?p=1000017#post1000017\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Anyway, I'm not really sure what I think about the book, so far. It kind of feels like how I felt about the Dark Ages 20th book in some ways. I really loved the style, the art, the visuals, but wasn't as sold on the writing. In this case, and this is completely subjective, I didn't really care for the vast majority of the magical sections dealing with Thaumaturgy styles. I don't know, I can't place my finger(s) on it, but it seemed like a large break from prior concepts and material for the sake of trying to push something new, but also comes off, at least on early reading as largely unplayable and unusable.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is very much how I feel about the Tome of Secrets. It is very well presented, and feels like it should be a useful book, but I have yet to find a single section which I feel actually enriches the game. One problem is that the sections on magic, which take up a large part of the book, present their contents in a fairly generic manner. Take Abyss Mysticism, for instance; the section discussing this starts with four paragraphs on &quot;The Horrors of Abyss Mysticism&quot;. Whilst this is not a bad notion in itself, said paragraphs amount to no more than telling us that the Abyss is a thing of horror. As the section tells us of the Lasombra:<div style=\"margin-left:40px\"><i>Their arts of shadow manipulation and drawing forth the primordial darkness rightly infect their foes with fear.</i></div> <br /> What is missing is any material to let us know what is so terrible about the Abyss and its darkness. There is nothing here which is sufficiently substantial to let the reader know why the enemies of the Lasombra should fear the darkness they are conjuring forth, rightly or otherwise. Not only is the writer not <i>showing</i> us, the readers, but the writer is barely even <i>telling</i> us, with a description that doesn't even touch the contextual background of the period. This, I think, is one reason why some readers are not connecting with the sections on magic; whilst a large proportion of older material for <i>Vampire: the Dark Ages</i> was background-led, with rules designed to actively bring the background into the game, these sections are very much rules-led, with a small amount of background to explain their inclusion in the book. The result is text which feels flat an insufficiently connected with the game it is designed to support.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/317-james_willoughby","name":"James_Willoughby","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar317_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-08T01:34:09-08:00","id":1000182,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Beckett</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/998155-v20-dark-ages-tome-of-secrets-discussion?p=1000017#post1000017\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Borderline like trying to get someone's own home game into published canon. But I'm not sure that's right, or to what extent, and there is certainly some degree of not liking change, especially as contradictions to, (or not knowing of), prior material. Some of it, like with the Koldun, I felt was a backwards step (and like I mentioned, gets very close to making it unusable), and I literally thought as I was reading it, &quot;someone is trying to make Sith Vampires&quot;.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I'll confess - as the writer of the Koldunic Sorcery section - to not actually liking or being terribly familiar with Star Wars. Never got on with the series. I found it horribly bland. Any similarities between Koldun and Sith is purely coincidental. My intention with that section (where Koldunic Sorcerers jealously guard their power) stems back to Tzimisce territoriality, the idea of the crotchety old mage in his tower, and to act as a reason for Tzimisce disunity when opposing the more organised and cohesive Tremere. I feel it stands up.<br /> <br /> By dint of my creating a lot of the material in this book from scratch, it is indeed effectively homebrew, but not material lifted from a home game. Everything I write attempts to expand the setting or elaborate on existing material - whether in major (we've got seeds of Harbinger of Skulls and Setite history in this book) or minor (Abyss Mysticism is likely only useable by Lasombra) ways. I attempt to be incredibly reverent to old material, mind you, and am well-versed in it.<br /> <br /> I'm more than comfortable with some readers being unhappy with my content, of course. I also never mind being questioned on what I've written <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> I write for players and Storytellers like me, and the members of my groups.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#000080\">Matthew Dawkins</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000080\">In-House Developer for Onyx Path Publishing</span></b><br /> <br /> <i><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b><span style=\"color:#008080\">Website: </span><a href=\"http://www.matthewdawkins.com\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.matthewdawkins.com</span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#008080\">Patreon: </span><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins</span></a></b></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/152-the-gentleman-gamer","name":"The Gentleman Gamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar152_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-08T01:34:50-08:00","id":1000183,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MachineIV</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/998155-v20-dark-ages-tome-of-secrets-discussion?p=999633#post999633\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Would you recommend any specific reading on the topic?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I would recommend that, if you want a section on the medieval night, you pay me to write it.<br /> <br /> (Sorry, limits to free advice do apply.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/317-james_willoughby","name":"James_Willoughby","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar317_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-08T01:37:39-08:00","id":1000184,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aahz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/998155-v20-dark-ages-tome-of-secrets-discussion?p=1000156#post1000156\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But according to the V20 rules, it is also a path used in Du-An-Ki, Wanga, Nahuallotl, New Age Blood Magic, Punk Sorcery and Hacktivist Thaumaturgy.<br /> <br /> If we ignore the Anarch Tarditions, the only Tremere paths that are not available for the other big traditions are The Green Path, Path of the Levinbolt and Path of Technomancy. (With the Anarchs they have no exclusive path left.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Absolutely, but note that I said &quot;that's how I run it,&quot; or words to that effect, not how the game <i>is</i>.<br /> <br /> That aside, I feel the Tremere have plenty of aspects that make them stand out from other blood magicians. Structure, rituals, more paths accessible than any other line of blood sorcerers, a rich history, a role in most domains, in-built social drama, and so on. To look at the Warlocks as weaker just because there are other blood magicians does their vast range of other aspects a disservice.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#000080\">Matthew Dawkins</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000080\">In-House Developer for Onyx Path Publishing</span></b><br /> <br /> <i><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b><span style=\"color:#008080\">Website: </span><a href=\"http://www.matthewdawkins.com\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.matthewdawkins.com</span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#008080\">Patreon: </span><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins</span></a></b></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/152-the-gentleman-gamer","name":"The Gentleman Gamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar152_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-08T01:41:15-08:00","id":1000186,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>James_Willoughby</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/998155-v20-dark-ages-tome-of-secrets-discussion?p=1000181#post1000181\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This is very much how I feel about the Tome of Secrets. It is very well presented, and feels like it should be a useful book, but I have yet to find a single section which I feel actually enriches the game. One problem is that the sections on magic, which take up a large part of the book, present their contents in a fairly generic manner. Take Abyss Mysticism, for instance; the section discussing this starts with four paragraphs on &quot;The Horrors of Abyss Mysticism&quot;. Whilst this is not a bad notion in itself, said paragraphs amount to no more than telling us that the Abyss is a thing of horror. As the section tells us of the Lasombra:<div style=\"margin-left:40px\"><i>Their arts of shadow manipulation and drawing forth the primordial darkness rightly infect their foes with fear.</i></div><br /> What is missing is any material to let us know what is so terrible about the Abyss and its darkness. There is nothing here which is sufficiently substantial to let the reader know why the enemies of the Lasombra should fear the darkness they are conjuring forth, rightly or otherwise. Not only is the writer not <i>showing</i> us, the readers, but the writer is barely even <i>telling</i> us, with a description that doesn't even touch the contextual background of the period. This, I think, is one reason why some readers are not connecting with the sections on magic; whilst a large proportion of older material for <i>Vampire: the Dark Ages</i> was background-led, with rules designed to actively bring the background into the game, these sections are very much rules-led, with a small amount of background to explain their inclusion in the book. The result is text which feels flat an insufficiently connected with the game it is designed to support.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I take your comments on board! Add details to that effect to the errata thread if you feel it's a big omission.<br /> <br /> I would counter that the denizens of the Abyss detailed in that same section <i>are</i> horrifying, even to vampires, and the powers described <i>are</i> disturbing, especially to vampires. A whirlpool to Oblivion opening in your nice safe haven while you sleep? That would make me fear the dark, even if I was a Cainite.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#000080\">Matthew Dawkins</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000080\">In-House Developer for Onyx Path Publishing</span></b><br /> <br /> <i><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b><span style=\"color:#008080\">Website: </span><a href=\"http://www.matthewdawkins.com\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.matthewdawkins.com</span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#008080\">Patreon: </span><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins</span></a></b></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/152-the-gentleman-gamer","name":"The Gentleman Gamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar152_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-08T02:27:01-08:00","id":1000193,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flower,Innocent</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/998155-v20-dark-ages-tome-of-secrets-discussion?p=999704#post999704\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Cad:<br /> Old Skool, Dur-an-ki, Sadhanna, Akhu and whatever are far older than thaumaturgy. Yes, it is a shame that most of their unique stuff is garbage (wanna play with shadows?) and I do thing countermagic shouldn't be a thaumaturgy only thing.<br /> other magics are much smaller. Much more limited, and much more individual .A punk wanting a new spell is going to go through a lot more effort than a tremere to get it.</div> </div> </div> </div>A lot of magick was older than Bonsagius' universal theory. It however united the majority of wizards of Europe and ultimately gave rise to the Technocracy. The advantage that the Order of Hermes brought and the Tremere for all their break away still have is they are very good at adapting other people's stuff and making it theirown. Something like Technomancy should be profoundly difficult for any of the ancient traditions to wrap their minds around. These are ancient traditions.<br /> <br /> The Advantage the Tremere have shouldn't be unique paths but rather they have the most options. WIth paths, with rituals etc. Other blood magics should have half or 1/3 the options.. and Tremere should always have the option to steal unique thaum they discover in game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-08T15:56:23-08:00","id":1000485,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>James_Willoughby</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/998155-v20-dark-ages-tome-of-secrets-discussion?p=1000183#post1000183\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I would recommend that, if you want a section on the medieval night, you pay me to write it.<br /> <br /> (Sorry, limits to free advice do apply.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Totally fair. I don't particularly have space for a section in anything I'm working on. I'd keep it in mind.<br /> <br /> I wasn't really asking for advice though. I was asking what you felt constituted good material on the topic because I wanted to better understand your stance. I went looking. I didn't find much beyond the obvious ones.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":70,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","user":"MachineIV","date":". 11-08-2016, 06:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-08T17:16:40-08:00","id":1000538,"title":"","content":"I feel like Guide to the high clans or one of the older supplements touched on medieval nights and winters. Something about the taverns being the only active places since there was no work in the off season. Also how festivals and war games would be important to vampires to maintain feeding stock.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2818-frostfox","name":"FrostFox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2818_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"264"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-08T17:53:50-08:00","id":1000552,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FrostFox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/998155-v20-dark-ages-tome-of-secrets-discussion?p=1000538#post1000538\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I feel like Guide to the high clans or one of the older supplements touched on medieval nights and winters. Something about the taverns being the only active places since there was no work in the off season. Also how festivals and war games would be important to vampires to maintain feeding stock.</div> </div> </div> </div>I actually had a bit written on how the concept of &quot;tavern&quot; we have in the modern days is a little off, how it was more a modular social service that was just one person or another's home for the time being. It got a bit wordy, so I didn't fit it. I figured, down the line I'd have space in companion material for that type of discussion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-09T16:42:29-08:00","id":1001071,"title":"","content":"Well, I just wanted to say that I am greatly pleased by the content in this book, it includes all that was promised and more while keeping an overall high quality and excellent writing as well as some really interesting design choices. My favourite parts are: Abyss Mysticism + Koldunic Sorcery and the Medieval Domain + Cainite Knightly Orders as well as Holy/Unholy Faith.<br /> <br /> I have always liked the concept of blood magic/sorcery with their rituals and paths but never really liked the Tremere or their style of Thaumaturgy. The main reason for this is that Tremere magic feels to all encompasing, possessing almost every path and ritual in existense and some unique ones but still lacking that special feeling when actually performing it, kinda feels like a Tremere just &quot;wills&quot; stuff to happen and it does, while Dur An Ki or Akhu are really interesting because of their religious ties and cultural differences. If possible I would like the Tremere to be sligthly more limited in their access to paths and especially rituals and instead gain some more unique paths only they have access to in order to give every school of blood magic something truly unique that separates and distinguishes them from each other. Trying to give the Tremere a specific way of going about when performing their magic as well as clearly defined limits to what they can achive with their blend of magic and not just saying its &quot;Hermetic Blood Socery&quot; would be ideal. Not much would be needed in wordcount, just some few sentences describing how they perform their magic and what differentiates their form of blood magic from other kinds of blood magic. This is of course my own opinion and everyones entiteled to their own but I really like lots of options and a rich and varied world with many variable concepts coexisting along and in some cases in opposition of each other.<br /> <br /> Since I am currently playing in a game in which my character, Matthew Smith, a generation 6 Kiasyd, is a prominent abyssal mystic and scholar whom have had over 1400 years to perfect his arts, this additional material on Abyss Mysticism was one of the things I looked forward to the most and I was not disappointed in the least. I really liked this part of the Tome of Secrets as well as the new Oubliette merit, however, if I might add one thought: Shouldnt any abyss mystic be able to &quot;attune&quot; with his own oubliette and grow accustomed to the presence of the abyss in there in order not to suffer any penalties when in his own sanctuary or lair? It just feels weird that an abyss mystic which is used to traveling in to the abyss and dealing with outerwordly forces would take the same penalty as someone of a particular road or whom has entered the oubliette of their free will but is lacking any relevant familarity or knowledge of the abyss and its denizens. Just one thing I thought about and found strange, no critizism intended. A small question for the awsome developers of V20-DA ToS. Could the Oubliette merit/background go above the printed rating of 5? For exsample: Could one have a minor underground settlement or even an underground city as ones oubliette with a rating of say 7-9?<br /> <br /> I will not go into detail about my thoughts on the other forms of blood sorceries but know that I am greatly impressed and happy to finally have the pdf in my hands.<br /> <br /> The feudal society + medieval fighting/warfare part was good reading and I felt it will very useful in the next game I will hold in the DA-setting.<br /> <br /> Really liked the information on the Cainite Knightly Orders.<br /> <br /> My favorite parts are the new and/or expanded chapter about faith, both Holy and Unholy in the dark medieval times.<br /> <br /> I feel many of the things mentioned in the book could be expanded even more in upcoming supplements and personally really hope they do.<br /> <br /> Thanks again for all the hard work, know that I really think that it shows just how amazing you guys are.<br /> <br /> As a final question: If people could add one more thing to this book, just one, be it a sentence or another chapter, regarding something you would like to include and think was missed or overlooked, what would that be and why? Mostly interested to hear what people like to see and read about in this type of books. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> With regards - Daniel P","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/533-daniel-p","name":"Daniel P","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar533_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"34"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-09T17:56:30-08:00","id":1001100,"title":"","content":"I'm not sure. A few things come to mind. Examples of play to show how some of the things are meant to work. A chapter on transitioning from Dark Ages to Modern, as Dark Ages did make some very major sweeping changes. A section focusing on real world historical religions and politics. Some ideas on how to use things (like Disciplines) a little out side of the box. A few intro stories with a few good hook possibilities.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://t0.gstatic.com/images?q=tbn:ANd9GcTAO8runv-CR5dodCXgw_8wdJype5yunYCODWdZiBAwUP5WFVv8\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://ksr-ugc.imgix.net/assets/003/593/392/92a29c2836b988505781770a32720148_original.png?v=1428699067&amp;w=700&amp;h=&amp;fit=max&amp;auto=format&amp;lossless=true&amp;s=69ffdde357a0cdd88ee89934622443f9\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img692/7017/hh2support.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img703/6636/6kvo.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1721-beckett","name":"Beckett","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1721_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1077"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-10T01:50:21-08:00","id":1001256,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/998155-v20-dark-ages-tome-of-secrets-discussion?p=1000193#post1000193\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Advantage the Tremere have shouldn't be unique paths but rather they have the most options. WIth paths, with rituals etc. Other blood magics should have half or 1/3 the options.. and Tremere should always have the option to steal unique thaum they discover in game.</div> </div> </div> </div>Having less options is not such a big deal as long if you have access to the good options, since the number of path and rituals is anyway way bigger than what a character can learn.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5199-aahz","name":"Aahz","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"610"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-10T02:08:41-08:00","id":1001264,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Daniel P</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/998155-v20-dark-ages-tome-of-secrets-discussion?p=1001071#post1001071\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, I just wanted to say that I am greatly pleased by the content in this book, it includes all that was promised and more while keeping an overall high quality and excellent writing as well as some really interesting design choices. My favourite parts are: Abyss Mysticism + Koldunic Sorcery and the Medieval Domain + Cainite Knightly Orders as well as Holy/Unholy Faith.<br /> <br /> I have always liked the concept of blood magic/sorcery with their rituals and paths but never really liked the Tremere or their style of Thaumaturgy. The main reason for this is that Tremere magic feels to all encompasing, possessing almost every path and ritual in existense and some unique ones but still lacking that special feeling when actually performing it, kinda feels like a Tremere just &amp;quot;wills&amp;quot; stuff to happen and it does, while Dur An Ki or Akhu are really interesting because of their religious ties and cultural differences. If possible I would like the Tremere to be sligthly more limited in their access to paths and especially rituals and instead gain some more unique paths only they have access to in order to give every school of blood magic something truly unique that separates and distinguishes them from each other. Trying to give the Tremere a specific way of going about when performing their magic as well as clearly defined limits to what they can achive with their blend of magic and not just saying its &amp;quot;Hermetic Blood Socery&amp;quot; would be ideal. Not much would be needed in wordcount, just some few sentences describing how they perform their magic and what differentiates their form of blood magic from other kinds of blood magic. This is of course my own opinion and everyones entiteled to their own but I really like lots of options and a rich and varied world with many variable concepts coexisting along and in some cases in opposition of each other.<br /> <br /> Since I am currently playing in a game in which my character, Matthew Smith, a generation 6 Kiasyd, is a prominent abyssal mystic and scholar whom have had over 1400 years to perfect his arts, this additional material on Abyss Mysticism was one of the things I looked forward to the most and I was not disappointed in the least. I really liked this part of the Tome of Secrets as well as the new Oubliette merit, however, if I might add one thought: Shouldnt any abyss mystic be able to &amp;quot;attune&amp;quot; with his own oubliette and grow accustomed to the presence of the abyss in there in order not to suffer any penalties when in his own sanctuary or lair? It just feels weird that an abyss mystic which is used to traveling in to the abyss and dealing with outerwordly forces would take the same penalty as someone of a particular road or whom has entered the oubliette of their free will but is lacking any relevant familarity or knowledge of the abyss and its denizens. Just one thing I thought about and found strange, no critizism intended. A small question for the awsome developers of V20-DA ToS. Could the Oubliette merit/background go above the printed rating of 5? For exsample: Could one have a minor underground settlement or even an underground city as ones oubliette with a rating of say 7-9?<br /> <br /> I will not go into detail about my thoughts on the other forms of blood sorceries but know that I am greatly impressed and happy to finally have the pdf in my hands.<br /> <br /> The feudal society + medieval fighting/warfare part was good reading and I felt it will very useful in the next game I will hold in the DA-setting.<br /> <br /> Really liked the information on the Cainite Knightly Orders.<br /> <br /> My favorite parts are the new and/or expanded chapter about faith, both Holy and Unholy in the dark medieval times.<br /> <br /> I feel many of the things mentioned in the book could be expanded even more in upcoming supplements and personally really hope they do.<br /> <br /> Thanks again for all the hard work, know that I really think that it shows just how amazing you guys are.<br /> <br /> As a final question: If people could add one more thing to this book, just one, be it a sentence or another chapter, regarding something you would like to include and think was missed or overlooked, what would that be and why? Mostly interested to hear what people like to see and read about in this type of books. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> With regards - Daniel P</div> </div> </div> </div>Glad you like the Abyss Mysticism! And I agree with your point on &quot;attuning&quot; to your own oubliette. I'll discuss with David and see if we can amend it. As for whether the Oubliette Background can go higher than five - I suppose it could, though the labyrinth containing multiple structures defined under the five point rating is in my mind at least a large village or small town. I was thinking of Castel d'Ombro when I wrote that, as I imagine it's a castle with all natural outlaying structures, and the like.<br /> <br /> As for what I'd add if I could contribute another chapter? Well, thankfully I've been able to add what I want to V20 Dark Ages Companion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#000080\">Matthew Dawkins</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000080\">In-House Developer for Onyx Path Publishing</span></b><br /> <br /> <i><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b><span style=\"color:#008080\">Website: </span><a href=\"http://www.matthewdawkins.com\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.matthewdawkins.com</span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#008080\">Patreon: </span><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins</span></a></b></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/152-the-gentleman-gamer","name":"The Gentleman Gamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar152_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-10T03:39:52-08:00","id":1001289,"title":"","content":"Does the book contain guides on transferring the powers to V20? Furthermore, do we get any more on the relationship between a Koldun and their Spirits? Any final confirmation on what these spirits (leleks, nature spirits etc.) are? Are they umbral spirits? Are they related to the spirits awoken and manipulated with Spiritus? Are they demons (lower case d, not the Fallen) or Banes? And Kupala? Earthbound? Demi-urge to Gaia? On the off-chance that you've never considered it <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/152-the-gentleman-gamer\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar152_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"152\" data-vbnamecard=\"152\">The Gentleman Gamer</a>, what do you think of Kupala as a dark side of Gaia? It would explain why the spirits of the earth are hospitable to both Fera and the Kolduns, and it would explain a lot of the conflict between the Tzimisce/Kupala and the Garou, the Garou being repelled out of Kupala's Lands, the Garou being in possession of Kupala's Sacred Fire Flower... Combine that with making the spirits of Koldunism banes and it could open up a lot of interesting antagonism between the Fera and the Tzimisce which goes beyond &quot;you have Wyrm Taint and so you must be destroyed&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11620,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","user":"twig","date":". 11-10-2016, 06:46 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-10T05:34:21-08:00","id":1001323,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/998155-v20-dark-ages-tome-of-secrets-discussion?p=1001289#post1001289\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does the book contain guides on transferring the powers to V20? Furthermore, do we get any more on the relationship between a Koldun and their Spirits? Any final confirmation on what these spirits (leleks, nature spirits etc.) are? Are they umbral spirits? Are they related to the spirits awoken and manipulated with Spiritus? Are they demons (lower case d, not the Fallen) or Banes? And Kupala? Earthbound? Demi-urge to Gaia? On the off-chance that you've never considered it <span class=\"b-bbcode-user js-bbcode-user\">Guest</span>, what do you think of Kupala as a dark side of Gaia? It would explain why the spirits of the earth are hospitable to both Fera and the Kolduns, and it would explain a lot of the conflict between the Tzimisce/Kupala and the Garou, the Garou being repelled out of Kupala's Lands, the Garou being in possession of Kupala's Sacred Fire Flower... Combine that with making the spirits of Koldunism banes and it could open up a lot of interesting antagonism between the Fera and the Tzimisce which goes beyond &amp;quot;you have Wyrm Taint and so you must be destroyed&amp;quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>The book seems to imply demon spirits of sorts, which compel the koldun to covet knowledge and pushes them toward rivalry and conflict with other koldun.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2818-frostfox","name":"FrostFox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2818_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"264"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-10T12:10:03-08:00","id":1001423,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hm8453a</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/998155-v20-dark-ages-tome-of-secrets-discussion?p=999713#post999713\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Historian here. I could write you several articles about how inaccurate both of those shows are.<br /> <br /> Unless you're saying their combat is historically accurate. I don't know shit about military history and also I don't care very much, but you're over here conflating military history with the overall accuracy of a setting. That's bullshit. Every single medievalist I know goes on rants when they see people talking about Vikings and Game of Thrones.</div> </div> </div> </div><i>Game of Thrones</i> has fire breathing dragons, ice zombies, psychically-bonded pet wolves and some geriatric witch giving birth to shadow demons. Somehow I suspect painstaking realism and historical accuracy weren't high on the list of priorities for that property.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-10T12:27:37-08:00","id":1001428,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Matt the Bruins fan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/998155-v20-dark-ages-tome-of-secrets-discussion?p=1001423#post1001423\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <i>Game of Thrones</i> has fire breathing dragons, ice zombies, psychically-bonded pet wolves and some geriatric witch giving birth to shadow demons. Somehow I suspect painstaking realism and historical accuracy weren't high on the list of priorities for that property.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, correct. Hence why no one should claim that it's historically accurate. This was a claim someone else made that I responded to.<br /> <br /> And even if we ignore the fantasy elements and look at the portrayal of medieval society, it is still not historically accurate. I'm confused as to why you quoted and responded to me, and not to the person who made the comment calling Game of Thrones historically accurate.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:12px\">-</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3093-hm8453a","name":"hm8453a","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3093_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"636"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-10T12:59:45-08:00","id":1001446,"title":"","content":"Because your post seemed to be calling out the show for not being accurate when it's pretty obvious it was never meant to be in the first place.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-10T13:03:30-08:00","id":1001448,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Matt the Bruins fan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/998155-v20-dark-ages-tome-of-secrets-discussion?p=1001446#post1001446\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because your post seemed to be calling out the show for not being accurate when it's pretty obvious it was never meant to be in the first place.</div> </div> </div> </div>In response to another poster who literally said, &quot;I felt like maybe the culture had shifted and there were more historical nerds online now, playing RPGs. We see more realistic depictions of medieval society and warfare more often now. From historical series like vikings to even fantasies like game of thrones.&quot;<br /> <br /> In response.<br /> <br /> I didn't come here out of nowhere and say, &quot;hey, y'all, you know what's not historically accurate? Game of Thrones&quot;. What the hell are we discussing?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:12px\">-</span>","edited":{"userid":3093,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3093-hm8453a","user":"hm8453a","date":". 11-10-2016, 04:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3093-hm8453a","name":"hm8453a","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3093_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"636"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-10T13:35:10-08:00","id":1001464,"title":"","content":"Well, it appears as if we're moving toward discussing excessive defensiveness about being replied to in a public conversation. You do get that my initial remark was an offhanded bit of levity, not an extensive critique of your historical expertise, right?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-10T13:47:01-08:00","id":1001468,"title":"","content":"What the hell is wrong with you people? Leave her alone. She hasn't done anything wrong, and you're just jumping at her. Leave her alone.<br /> <br /> I am ashamed of her fellow writers on this thread who have yet to support their coworker. She's not saying anything about it, but I can't imagine it's very easy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>International Relations Scholar, Salesman, and GM. Guess which one of those is my favorite?","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12305-obrimosmaintenance","name":"ObrimosMaintenance","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-10T13:50:12-08:00","id":1001473,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ObrimosMaintenance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/998155-v20-dark-ages-tome-of-secrets-discussion?p=1001468#post1001468\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What the hell is wrong with you people? Leave her alone. She hasn't done anything wrong, and you're just jumping at her. Leave her alone.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks. They're on my ignore list, but I appreciate it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:12px\">-</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3093-hm8453a","name":"hm8453a","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3093_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"636"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-10T14:28:43-08:00","id":1001491,"title":"","content":"Historian here (my field is Legal History, however). I have two book suggestions for those interested in what people living in pre-industrial or pre-gas lamps Europe did with their nights:<br /> - Evening's Empire: A History of the Night in Early Modern Europe (by Craig Koslofsky); and<br /> - At Day's Close: Night in Time's Past (by Robert Ekirch).<br /> <br /> Unfortunately, I have no suggestions on the 13th century (my period of interest being the 18th century), but if you don't care about anachronism, well, these two books are fine enough.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1119-primal-flame","name":"Primal Flame","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1119_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"230"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-10T15:18:00-08:00","id":1001518,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ObrimosMaintenance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/998155-v20-dark-ages-tome-of-secrets-discussion?p=1001468#post1001468\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am ashamed of her fellow writers on this thread who have yet to support their coworker. She's not saying anything about it, but I can't imagine it's very easy.</div> </div> </div> </div>I do not underestimate Hayley's ability and determination. She's one of the toughest cookies I know, and she's handled far worse than what this thread's handed to her. All of us writers are capable of handling criticism or debate to some extent or other, and we have a good enough network that if one of us did need assistance, we could speak to one another about it. I've every confidence in Hayley not needing one of us to step in.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#000080\">Matthew Dawkins</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000080\">In-House Developer for Onyx Path Publishing</span></b><br /> <br /> <i><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b><span style=\"color:#008080\">Website: </span><a href=\"http://www.matthewdawkins.com\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.matthewdawkins.com</span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#008080\">Patreon: </span><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins</span></a></b></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/152-the-gentleman-gamer","name":"The Gentleman Gamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar152_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-11T02:14:18-08:00","id":1001683,"title":"","content":"So I have a question regarding the Revelations of Duat, I'm hoping that I'm just being dumb because I've been reading at 5am, but still. So I understand the first two dots just fine, see ghost and read ghosts soul to find 'shards' to latch onto for the 3-5 dot powers. My confusion comes from how long the corpses/mummies can last because it mentions that each success makes the corpse do as it's told for an additional night, then a paragraph over it says that the corpses will be permanently active and never compose only to then say after the corpses states that it crumbles to dust upon using it's blood pool. So how long can a corpse be active? Does the corpse become inactive once the night is over because the soul shard returns to the ghost? Is it just no longer under the Setites control? Further more is the 3 dot versions blood pool only for healing/buffs because in the Sorcery of LIfe it mentions that if a 'Proto-bane Mummy' (Kinda love this, even if my knowledge of mummy is suuuper lacking) loses it's soul shard it becomes a unthinking sentry no longer capable of using it's disciplines which are bot 'physical' disciplines with passive abilities. Are only the intelligent mummies allowed to use the active forms of disciplines like Fortitude and potency (Assuming that some high rolls can get them the more 'magical' disciplines with no passive abilities) if so what use is blood to the lower tiers? <br /> <br /> I deeply apologize if I have missed something or am showing a complete lack of reading comprehension, but I like the 'path' and wish to understand it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5604-faster-than-fedex","name":"Faster-Than-FedEx","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-11T05:00:22-08:00","id":1001715,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Faster-Than-FedEx</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/998155-v20-dark-ages-tome-of-secrets-discussion?p=1001683#post1001683\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So I have a question regarding the Revelations of Duat, I'm hoping that I'm just being dumb because I've been reading at 5am, but still. So I understand the first two dots just fine, see ghost and read ghosts soul to find 'shards' to latch onto for the 3-5 dot powers. My confusion comes from how long the corpses/mummies can last because it mentions that each success makes the corpse do as it's told for an additional night, then a paragraph over it says that the corpses will be permanently active and never compose only to then say after the corpses states that it crumbles to dust upon using it's blood pool. So how long can a corpse be active? Does the corpse become inactive once the night is over because the soul shard returns to the ghost? Is it just no longer under the Setites control? Further more is the 3 dot versions blood pool only for healing/buffs because in the Sorcery of LIfe it mentions that if a 'Proto-bane Mummy' (Kinda love this, even if my knowledge of mummy is suuuper lacking) loses it's soul shard it becomes a unthinking sentry no longer capable of using it's disciplines which are bot 'physical' disciplines with passive abilities. Are only the intelligent mummies allowed to use the active forms of disciplines like Fortitude and potency (Assuming that some high rolls can get them the more 'magical' disciplines with no passive abilities) if so what use is blood to the lower tiers? <br /> <br /> I deeply apologize if I have missed something or am showing a complete lack of reading comprehension, but I like the 'path' and wish to understand it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm glad you like it! I really enjoyed writing the Setite Sorcery. <br /> <br /> It may be sentence structure in this case. With one success, the power animates a corpse that's been dead for a single night. With two successes, the power animates a corpse that's been dead for two nights. And so on. So where it says &quot;for an additional night&quot; it doesn't mean &quot;It's animated for an additional night&quot; but &quot;a corpse dead for an additional night requires additional successes in order to animate.&quot; the crux is that the Setite has an easier time of it with a fresh corpse, probably recently murdered by the vampire. <br /> <br /> On the three-dot power I would only allow blood point use for passive activity, so you are quite correct.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#000080\">Matthew Dawkins</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000080\">In-House Developer for Onyx Path Publishing</span></b><br /> <br /> <i><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b><span style=\"color:#008080\">Website: </span><a href=\"http://www.matthewdawkins.com\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.matthewdawkins.com</span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#008080\">Patreon: </span><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins</span></a></b></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/152-the-gentleman-gamer","name":"The Gentleman Gamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar152_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-11T08:09:46-08:00","id":1001761,"title":"","content":"Out of curiosity does this book contain new paths or like Rites of Blood updated versions of older material?<br /> And how many and which path does it contain?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5199-aahz","name":"Aahz","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"610"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-11T08:29:38-08:00","id":1001769,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aahz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/998155-v20-dark-ages-tome-of-secrets-discussion?p=1001761#post1001761\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Out of curiosity does this book contain new paths or like Rites of Blood updated versions of older material?<br /> And how many and which path does it contain?</div> </div> </div> </div>There are new Paths. They're connected to Setite Sorcery and Koldunism, but if you're particularly eager, you can always adapt them to be regular Thuamaturgy. They have specific focus on the clans that wield them, but there's nothing to stop the toolkit ST making them accessible to other clans. This book contains no older material, to my knowledge.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#000080\">Matthew Dawkins</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000080\">In-House Developer for Onyx Path Publishing</span></b><br /> <br /> <i><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b><span style=\"color:#008080\">Website: </span><a href=\"http://www.matthewdawkins.com\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.matthewdawkins.com</span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#008080\">Patreon: </span><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins</span></a></b></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/152-the-gentleman-gamer","name":"The Gentleman Gamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar152_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-11T09:10:38-08:00","id":1001791,"title":"","content":"Ah, alright thank you Matthew for explaining. Otherwise I very much enjoy the Abyssal Mysticism stuff, even if I'm not sure I can use it for my dark ages lasombra, bit to 'unchristian' for what I imagine a path of heavens vampire would tolerate using. I also suuuuper loved the Holy (and unholy stuff, though to a lesser degree) stuff, just wish there was more in the chapter, it's a topic I rather enjoy!<br /> <br /> Also, long time fan (Bought two books from you as well) of yours Matthew, really happy to be seeing your name in books and getting a chance to read your stuff! Can't wait to see more stuff from you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5604-faster-than-fedex","name":"Faster-Than-FedEx","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-11T09:49:26-08:00","id":1001816,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Faster-Than-FedEx</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/998155-v20-dark-ages-tome-of-secrets-discussion?p=1001791#post1001791\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ah, alright thank you Matthew for explaining. Otherwise I very much enjoy the Abyssal Mysticism stuff, even if I'm not sure I can use it for my dark ages lasombra, bit to 'unchristian' for what I imagine a path of heavens vampire would tolerate using. I also suuuuper loved the Holy (and unholy stuff, though to a lesser degree) stuff, just wish there was more in the chapter, it's a topic I rather enjoy!<br /> <br /> Also, long time fan (Bought two books from you as well) of yours Matthew, really happy to be seeing your name in books and getting a chance to read your stuff! Can't wait to see more stuff from you.</div> </div> </div> </div>Gratifying to hear you enjoy my work! Thanks!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#000080\">Matthew Dawkins</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000080\">In-House Developer for Onyx Path Publishing</span></b><br /> <br /> <i><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b><span style=\"color:#008080\">Website: </span><a href=\"http://www.matthewdawkins.com\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.matthewdawkins.com</span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#008080\">Patreon: </span><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins</span></a></b></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/152-the-gentleman-gamer","name":"The Gentleman Gamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar152_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-11T14:38:19-08:00","id":1001937,"title":"","content":"How is Infernalism/Dark Thaumaturgy/Diamonion handled. Evil and faith takes up a chapter. <br /> <br /> Like, they've never been consistent. There's always been an agenda behind them. Sometimes they're unplayable mustache twirlers and you're evil just for being sired into the wrong clan. The last black hand book had moraly grey baali, and the last rites of the blood book went full mixed bag. (using diamonion reduces all roads but Evil revelations per use. Whut?)<br /> <br /> There's never been a good/balanced system for demonic investments.<br /> <br /> There's been some fluff, but few rules, on enslaving demons and coming out on top. Using true names and whatnot, stealing their power against their will. So on.<br /> <br /> I've always felt that Diamonion, being a discipline, shouldn't be any different from the 40 other disciplines. You shouldn't be especially damned for having it, even if it draws power from hell or torment. You trade your soul for investments and blood magic, not disciplines of the blood<br /> (and, well, anyone can ask for investments without a discipline, so logically Diamonion 6 should be someone safely investing in themselves through the blood, right?)<br /> <br /> And, well, some fluff outright says that many baali refuse to bow to demons, so you'd think they'd have developed a different discipline if that were true. I mean, scaring other people into thinking your power is evil and damning is great and all in keeping it secret and exclusive, but sucks if it's true, amrite?<br /> <br /> Does dark thaumaturgy now blend better into other blood magic schools, or is it thaumaturgy? There was a nice bit In the black hand book about demons in Dur-an-ki, for instance<br /> <br /> I mean, I like the odd, unredeamably evil baali. I think Diamonion actually has potential for good (if you want to be the kind of self-righteous paladin that goes too far) but, socially, most people who deal with demons are going to want the upper hand. They think they can walk the tightrope. And if you're really clever, maybe that tightrope can hold you up. A lot of vampires are very intellegent and very patient, they could do it if nobody else can. That tightrope offers a lot of interesting rollplay. At the very least, I can imagine some baali just don't care for demonic masters, pretend to be some other clan, and live their unlives like regular jackoffs.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Signatures are for terrible people who want to be caught.","edited":{"userid":12414,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12414-flower-innocent","user":"Flower,Innocent","date":". 11-12-2016, 09:52 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12414-flower-innocent","name":"Flower,Innocent","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12414_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"268"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-12T03:16:29-08:00","id":1002168,"title":"","content":"I'm going to be showing off my ignorance, but where do I buy the PDF from? :')<br /> The book sounds great, and I'm a sucker for kool powerz, so I'm going to buy the PDF at the first opportunity. Is it available yet?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-12T06:18:03-08:00","id":1002196,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/998155-v20-dark-ages-tome-of-secrets-discussion?p=1002168#post1002168\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm going to be showing off my ignorance, but where do I buy the PDF from? :')<br /> The book sounds great, and I'm a sucker for kool powerz, so I'm going to buy the PDF at the first opportunity. Is it available yet?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not available to the general public yet. It has been released as an advanced PDF to those who backed the kickstarter for V20DA. Once the errata has been incorporated into the book it will be released at DrivethruRPG.com","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imageshack.com/i/j5vvlqp\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/j5vvlqp\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/ghw20supporterhiddengaroup\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/n18segp\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0v25ewp\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">English is not my native language, so i apologize for errors in grammar or spelling.</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/392-cadmiumcadamium","name":"Cadmiumcadamium","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar392_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"936"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-12T07:21:22-08:00","id":1002209,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/392-cadmiumcadamium\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar392_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"392\" data-vbnamecard=\"392\">Cadmiumcadamium</a> Thanks! Can't wait","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-13T10:14:07-08:00","id":1002553,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hm8453a</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/998155-v20-dark-ages-tome-of-secrets-discussion?p=1001448#post1001448\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In response to another poster who literally said, &quot;I felt like maybe the culture had shifted and there were more historical nerds online now, playing RPGs. We see <b>more realistic</b> depictions of medieval society and warfare more often now. From historical series like vikings to even <b>fantasies</b> like game of thrones.&quot;<br /> In response.<br /> I didn't come here out of nowhere and say, &quot;hey, y'all, you know what's not historically accurate? Game of Thrones&quot;. What the hell are we discussing?</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Matt the Bruins fan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/998155-v20-dark-ages-tome-of-secrets-discussion?p=1001464#post1001464\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, it appears as if we're moving toward discussing excessive defensiveness about being replied to in a public conversation. You do get that my initial remark was an offhanded bit of levity, not an extensive critique of your historical expertise, right?</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Daniel P</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/998155-v20-dark-ages-tome-of-secrets-discussion?p=1001071#post1001071\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As a final question: If people could add one more thing to this book, just one, be it a sentence or another chapter, regarding something you would like to include and think was missed or overlooked, what would that be and why? Mostly interested to hear what people like to see and read about in this type of books. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe it's just me, but this sounds like something that might make for a really good future Vampire/Dark Ages product to tackle? This sort of thing is generally why I prefer Revised era material over everything else, as it really went out of it's way to marry a degree of historical or real world accuracy with the game's and setting's fantastic possibilities (without generally trying to whitewash or degrade the setting material).<br /> <br /> So, in hopes of cutting off the seemingly odd hot button discussion (what the hell guys/gals), <i>who would be interested in this sort of product?</i> Either as an extra chapter in Tome of Secrets, (unlikely due to time) or as another future book, or even section in a future book?<br /> <br /> <i>What sorts of things would you like to see or have covered?<br /> <br /> How high a priority would something like this be on your proverbial &quot;Take My Money&quot; wishlist?</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://t0.gstatic.com/images?q=tbn:ANd9GcTAO8runv-CR5dodCXgw_8wdJype5yunYCODWdZiBAwUP5WFVv8\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://ksr-ugc.imgix.net/assets/003/593/392/92a29c2836b988505781770a32720148_original.png?v=1428699067&amp;w=700&amp;h=&amp;fit=max&amp;auto=format&amp;lossless=true&amp;s=69ffdde357a0cdd88ee89934622443f9\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img692/7017/hh2support.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img703/6636/6kvo.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":1721,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1721-beckett","user":"Beckett","date":". 11-13-2016, 01:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1721-beckett","name":"Beckett","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1721_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1077"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-13T13:06:51-08:00","id":1002617,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Gentleman Gamer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/998155-v20-dark-ages-tome-of-secrets-discussion?p=999688#post999688\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I would say that the core book has the generic, accessible weapons chart most players expect and desire. To get more granular may confuse or irritate players looking for something quick and easy.<br /> <br /> Luckily for you, Dark Ages Companion goes into thorough detail on period appropriate weaponry and armour, so a hurrah for that!</div> </div> </div> </div>Would be good to see! I got more and more cringy seeing otherwise good games strengthening the old, old wrong assumptions of rpgs regarding weapons and combat.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2