om Aludian to Zettler!</div> </div> </div> </div>who are they?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3241-stannis","name":"Stannis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3241_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"115"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-14T08:00:48-08:00","id":1002888,"title":"","content":"Both of them are secret Infernalists. Aludian Thex is a Lasombra of the Antitribu I believe, and Zettler is a Malkavian Antitribu Elder, Methuselah level, who is a Director on the Board of Pentex, with Thex as a Puppet Master for another Board Member.<br /> <br /> Lot of Cool references in this book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-14T10:25:51-08:00","id":1002943,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/998155-v20-dark-ages-tome-of-secrets-discussion?p=1002888#post1002888\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Both of them are secret Infernalists. Aludian Thex is a Lasombra of the Antitribu I believe, and Zettler is a Malkavian Antitribu Elder, Methuselah level, who is a Director on the Board of Pentex, with Thex as a Puppet Master for another Board Member.<br /> <br /> Lot of Cool references in this book.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm glad someone caught those <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> There are others. I do enjoy easter eggs.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#000080\">Matthew Dawkins</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000080\">In-House Developer for Onyx Path Publishing</span></b><br /> <br /> <i><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b><span style=\"color:#008080\">Website: </span><a href=\"http://www.matthewdawkins.com\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.matthewdawkins.com</span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#008080\">Patreon: </span><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins</span></a></b></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/152-the-gentleman-gamer","name":"The Gentleman Gamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar152_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-23T05:11:01-08:00","id":1007174,"title":"","content":"So, With the sticky gone, Is this close to release?<br /> <br /> /also. Can someone satisfy my need for infernal feedback?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Signatures are for terrible people who want to be caught.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12414-flower-innocent","name":"Flower,Innocent","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12414_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"268"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-23T10:32:22-08:00","id":1007312,"title":"","content":"Yeah, when will we get hour hands on it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12142-undead-rabbit","name":"Undead rabbit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-23T17:35:25-08:00","id":1007500,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flower,Innocent</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/998155-v20-dark-ages-tome-of-secrets-discussion?p=1007174#post1007174\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, With the sticky gone, Is this close to release?<br /> <br /> /also. Can someone satisfy my need for infernal feedback?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's ... close?<br /> <br /> I just handed a pretty massive errata pile over to our layout team to integrate. So, it'll basically come down to when they get that done. No estimates.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-24T18:20:01-08:00","id":1007894,"title":"","content":"Has the Road of the Hive of Road of Night shown up in any VDA20 material?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-25T13:15:37-08:00","id":1008246,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vertical8</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/998155-v20-dark-ages-tome-of-secrets-discussion?p=1002621#post1002621\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Am I the only one who can't make heads or tails of the &quot;By Oath of Fealty&quot; section on page 78? I've read it a few times and can't wrap my head around how the mechanics are supposed to work.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I didn't write that section (I did knights) and it is, honestly a bit mangled, but I can summarize it for you:<br /> <br /> 1) The liege gives the vassal Background dots that can be combined with the vassal's for an Anchor background, in exchange for twice as many dots from the vassal for their own use.<br /> 2) The liege's dots are worth half as much (rounded up) when pooled for Anchor Background purposes.<br /> 3) The pooled vassal/liege Background cannot exceed the liege's rating.<br /> 4) But the liege can provide the same Background dots multiple times -- as many as their rating -- without using up the Background.<br /> 5) Terms may be set that replace a certain number of Background dots granted by vassals.<br /> <br /> The systems for knights are based on this last point. For instance, instead of providing 6 dots to a liege, a veteran knight (or someone who everyone thinks is one) only needs to provide 3 + the reputation/service's value of 3 dots. For Cainites, being a vampire is a benefit of this kind on its own. For example, a vampire willing to shed blood in service is considered to provide a value equivalent to 4 dots.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Writer, Game Designer, Pro since 99.<br /> <br /> Thoughts at <a href=\"http://mobunited.com\" target=\"_blank\">mobunited.com</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/164-malcolm","name":"Malcolm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar164_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-25T13:23:23-08:00","id":1008249,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malcolm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/998155-v20-dark-ages-tome-of-secrets-discussion?p=1008246#post1008246\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I didn't write that section (I did knights) and it is, honestly a bit mangled, but I can summarize it for you:<br /> <br /> 1) The liege gives the vassal Background dots that can be combined with the vassal's for an Anchor background, in exchange for twice as many dots from the vassal for their own use.<br /> 2) The liege's dots are worth half as much (rounded up) when pooled for Anchor Background purposes.<br /> 3) The pooled vassal/liege Background cannot exceed the liege's rating.<br /> 4) But the liege can provide the same Background dots multiple times -- as many as their rating -- without using up the Background.<br /> 5) Terms may be set that replace a certain number of Background dots granted by vassals.<br /> <br /> The systems for knights are based on this last point. For instance, instead of providing 6 dots to a liege, a veteran knight (or someone who everyone thinks is one) only needs to provide 3 + the reputation/service's value of 3 dots. For Cainites, being a vampire is a benefit of this kind on its own. For example, a vampire willing to shed blood in service is considered to provide a value equivalent to 4 dots.</div> </div> </div> </div>Can you make an example showing what everybody is providing an can use in the end?<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5199-aahz","name":"Aahz","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"610"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-25T21:46:54-08:00","id":1008411,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aahz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/998155-v20-dark-ages-tome-of-secrets-discussion?p=1008249#post1008249\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can you make an example showing what everybody is providing an can use in the end?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Again, this is not my section, but:<br /> <br /> Sir John of Dover, a veteran knight (2 dots of reputation for terms) offers Resources 2, Retainers 2 and Influence 2 to Arnott, Duke of Kent -- that's 6 dots of Backgrounds and 2 equivalent points in terms. The Duke offers Resources 4 in return, of which 2 dots is added to Sir John's total.<br /> <br /> Sir John now accesses Resources 4.<br /> <br /> The Duke accesses Resources 6, pools Sir John's Backgrounds with his own or can otherwise call on them, and Sir John himself must provide 40 days of military service a year for the Duke. <br /> <br /> Now if they were treating each other as social equals they would pool their Backgrounds normally instead, but the advantage here is really that Arnott can build this relationship with multiple vassals without having his Resources Background used up by these commitments.<br /> <br /> As I said, I didn't write this section, but one thing I'd note totally unofficially is that even though a liege can use the same Anchor to support multiple vassals, those vassals' contributions in return should not stack, or else the liege's Backgrounds will really get out of hand. I'd say the liege gets the best pool out of all contributing vassals instead. If you want to get really technical you might say that each additional vassal that would have increased the value instead provides a -1 difficulty break to rolls using that Background in conditions where it would make sense.<br /> <br /> Another question that needs answering is pooling of the non-Anchor Backgrounds -- does it work both ways, so the vassal can gain from them when pooled with the liege's? I'd say the answer is &quot;yes,&quot; and that this half-rating grant of the liege's rating is consistent throughout.<br /> <br /> For example, Arnott may possess Retainers 2 and Influence 3, and pooled with Sir John's offerings, this increases to 4 and 5, respectively, but Sir John only accesses 3 (his + half the Duke's rating) and 4 (same, rounded up). This makes vassalage a bit of a better deal.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Writer, Game Designer, Pro since 99.<br /> <br /> Thoughts at <a href=\"http://mobunited.com\" target=\"_blank\">mobunited.com</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/164-malcolm","name":"Malcolm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar164_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-26T03:37:58-08:00","id":1008471,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/164-malcolm\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar164_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"164\" data-vbnamecard=\"164\">Malcolm</a> <br /> Thanks, I think it would really help if there was an example like this (maybe better one with more than one Vassal) in the final book (but that is probably to late now).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5199-aahz","name":"Aahz","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"610"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-26T06:40:50-08:00","id":1008512,"title":"","content":"See. That seems a little weak (or you're not explaining well). Like, Adding up retainers and the like is fine and all, but resource dots go up exponentially. Like, I think in modern pounds we worked out that 1 dot is 15k a year, 2 dots is 30k. 3 dots is 120k. 4 dots is somewhere between 500k a year and a low million.5 dots is a few million a year of personal finances. Or, well, They get vaguer as you work your way out, and I confess my previous numbers seemed more accurate than what I've posted now.<br /> <br /> But. The point is. 3 dots of resources+ 3 dots of resources might equal 4 dots of resources if you're lucky. They don't equal five and they certainly don't equal six.<br /> <br /> I think a safe thing. Is that each level is the last level's worth, times it's level.<br /> <br /> IE. 2 dots is double 1 dot<br /> 3 dots is tripple 2 dots. <br /> 6 dots is 6 times 5th dot.<br /> <br /> If you're fine with boring your game with maths. This means that three two dot resources can form a third dot. Six one dot resources can make a third dot. and so on. For at least domain and resources.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Signatures are for terrible people who want to be caught.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12414-flower-innocent","name":"Flower,Innocent","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12414_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"268"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-27T09:28:15-08:00","id":1008950,"title":"","content":"Can someone explain, if it's allowed, the secret behind Koldunic sorcery?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2768-zorker","name":"Zorker","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-28T02:00:12-08:00","id":1009240,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Flower,Innocent</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/998155-v20-dark-ages-tome-of-secrets-discussion?p=1008512#post1008512\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">See. That seems a little weak (or you're not explaining well). Like, Adding up retainers and the like is fine and all, but resource dots go up exponentially. Like, I think in modern pounds we worked out that 1 dot is 15k a year, 2 dots is 30k. 3 dots is 120k. 4 dots is somewhere between 500k a year and a low million.5 dots is a few million a year of personal finances. Or, well, They get vaguer as you work your way out, and I confess my previous numbers seemed more accurate than what I've posted now.<br /> <br /> But. The point is. 3 dots of resources+ 3 dots of resources might equal 4 dots of resources if you're lucky. They don't equal five and they certainly don't equal six.<br /> <br /> I think a safe thing. Is that each level is the last level's worth, times it's level.<br /> <br /> IE. 2 dots is double 1 dot<br /> 3 dots is tripple 2 dots.<br /> 6 dots is 6 times 5th dot.<br /> <br /> If you're fine with boring your game with maths. This means that three two dot resources can form a third dot. Six one dot resources can make a third dot. and so on. For at least domain and resources.</div> </div> </div> </div>There is general the problem that some background grow exponentally and some don't (and in case of Gerd the size of the Herd grows exponetially but the blood they provide linearly which makes no sense at all).<br /> <br /> And even among the more linear Backgrounds there are some that profite from pooling and some that don't. Having one big Domain is imo better than several small ones, while for a Herd it doesn't really make a difference.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5199,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5199-aahz","user":"Aahz","date":". 11-28-2016, 05:07 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5199-aahz","name":"Aahz","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"610"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-24T19:28:06-08:00","id":1021767,"title":"","content":"Just for fun, I did a little analysis. Here's how the space usage of ToS breaks down:<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://i.gyazo.com/47257dab7c8ec836aa95e7e8c94638e7.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> So...I'm seeing a lot of Thaumaturgy creep. When more than 52% of a supplement is dedicated to expanding the capabilities of blood sorcery, you can clearly see where the focus of the writers is.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I seem to have acquired a site for running play by post games. This is unexpected and frightening and come watch either the glorious play or the magnificent train wreck:<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://madnessforums.com/forums/index.php\" target=\"_blank\">The Malkavian Madness Network</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1515-benjcano","name":"BenjCano","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1515_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1276"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-24T19:50:24-08:00","id":1021774,"title":"","content":"To be fair, isn't ToS supposed to be a book dedicated to blood sorcery? With nothing for the original blood mages(still salty), but still.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11512-zanos","name":"Zanos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11512_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"550"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-24T20:57:59-08:00","id":1021803,"title":"","content":"I assumed it was suppossed to be more along the lines of the Book of Storyteller Secrets, but here is the description from Drivethru.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Drivethru RPG</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Tome of Secrets is a treatment of numerous topics about Cainites and stranger things in the Dark Medieval World. It\u2019s about peeling back the curtain, and digging a little deeper. Inside, you\u2019ll find: <br /> Expanded treatment of Assamite Sorcery, Koldunic Sorcery, Necromancy, and Setite Sorcery <br /> A look at Cainite knightly orders, faith movements, and even human witchcraft <br /> Letters and diaries from all over the Dark Medieval World<br /> This book was made possible by the backers of the Deluxe V20 Dark Ages Kickstarter.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://t0.gstatic.com/images?q=tbn:ANd9GcTAO8runv-CR5dodCXgw_8wdJype5yunYCODWdZiBAwUP5WFVv8\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://ksr-ugc.imgix.net/assets/003/593/392/92a29c2836b988505781770a32720148_original.png?v=1428699067&amp;w=700&amp;h=&amp;fit=max&amp;auto=format&amp;lossless=true&amp;s=69ffdde357a0cdd88ee89934622443f9\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img692/7017/hh2support.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img703/6636/6kvo.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1721-beckett","name":"Beckett","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1721_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1077"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-25T00:27:05-08:00","id":1021883,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zanos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/998155-v20-dark-ages-tome-of-secrets-discussion?p=1021774#post1021774\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To be fair, isn't ToS supposed to be a book dedicated to blood sorcery? With nothing for the original blood mages(still salty), but still.</div> </div> </div> </div>Don't we already have three or fourother books dedicated to blood sorcery?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11891-rumata","name":"Rumata","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11891_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"602"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-25T04:05:34-08:00","id":1021928,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rumata</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/998155-v20-dark-ages-tome-of-secrets-discussion?p=1021883#post1021883\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Don't we already have three or fourother books dedicated to blood sorcery?</div> </div> </div> </div>The justification for making books on blood sorcery is that it's such a hot topic among power-gamers and is easy to abuse. That's literally part of the intro to one of them (Blood Sacrifice I think?). The issue is that each of these supplements makes Thaumaturgy more flexible and therefore more powerful. There is a blood magic power for every problem, and while that's kind of the point (necessity being the dark mother of magical invention), it still feels... like an issue.<br /> <br /> These books try and make Blood Magic less OP, by suggesting systems for EXP spending on rituals, stricter material requirements, even some vague fluff about blood magic being bad for your Humanity rating (and giving no system for it, wow, thanks... great to know that Power A reduces my humanity &quot;just because&quot;... and &quot;you spend hours isolated in study&quot; is not a valid reason btw).<br /> <br /> Next core edition just needs to have EXP costs for rituals. 3 Free rituals with each dot of Thaumaturgy, and all other rituals cost 1x level to master (minus the value of your Library, down to a minimum of 1). This would give a good reason for the Tremere being the &quot;best&quot; in modern WoD when it comes to Blood Magic. They have the best libraries, by a long haul. Almost every Chantry has a level 3 or higher library, and mentors are abundant. That along with collaboration due to the vinculu- I mean blood bond.<br /> <br /> All I can say is that Blood Magic is a great tool for powerful NPCs, and lots of the powers presented feel NPC-only. Creating Mummies, destroying buildings from afar... Akhu feels like villain material in a lot of ways. STs just need to be sensible and say &quot;yes, these powers exist, yes they're powerful, no, noone in this chronicle knows it&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11620,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","user":"twig","date":". 12-25-2016, 07:10 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-25T14:47:09-08:00","id":1022096,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rumata</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/998155-v20-dark-ages-tome-of-secrets-discussion?p=1021883#post1021883\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Don't we already have three or fourother books dedicated to blood sorcery?</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think we do for v20? I could be wrong.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11512-zanos","name":"Zanos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11512_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"550"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-25T14:54:53-08:00","id":1022098,"title":"","content":"We got Rites of the Blood. Which is most of the material from blood sercrets and blood sacrifice, So expanded paths and rituals for thaumaturgy and necromancy. Plus some stuff on setite sorcery and Dur-an-ki. Little bit on dark thaumturgy as wekk","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>1","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27-ulfsarkar","name":"Ulfsarkar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"86"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-25T16:03:13-08:00","id":1022110,"title":"","content":"All around I thought the book was very well written I have a few nit picks here and there but nothing that taking out of the game would destroy everything. For example I thought the concept of Wyrm Dark Thaumaturgy was a bit off for me, now I have nothing against other ST's using the Wyrm in their games far be it from me to tell them how to DM. But I personally will probably never ever use it because I have a huge disdain for Apocalypse as a whole. I do love the new Koldunic and Nercomantic powers added into the game because while Koldunic powers are dying off in my storyline the players are on the 4th crusade against Rustovich's allies and I wanted to show a wider range of powers the Kolduns possess over the earth itself. I do feel the Tremere where left out a bit but at the same time I think over the years there has been so much written about clan Tremere that it is alright they where left out mostly for this. Now I hope at some point the Telyavelic Tremere get an updated write up (and I hope the mention of Demons is left out when Telyavel is spoken of ho-hum) because I like the concept of animistic Tremere who sort of have a grasp on the concept of a kind of animistic necromancy. But back to the book I like it and hope for more content similar to it for dark ages in the coming future.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10343-the-anubi","name":"The Anubi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10343_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"116"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-25T16:05:38-08:00","id":1022113,"title":"","content":"<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zanos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/998155-v20-dark-ages-tome-of-secrets-discussion?p=1022096#post1022096\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't think we do for v20? I could be wrong.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, there are 'only' two books dedicated to blood magic in V20 (Rites and Tome of Secrets, since more than 50% of it is dedicated to that). But consider threat almost every book released since V20 has has dedicated significant portions of their word count to blood sorcery.<br /> <br /> Guide to the Tal'Mahe'Ra? Let's throw in 7 pages of Dark Thaumaturgy, 3 pages on a new form of Blood Magic we'll call Itarajana, some modernization of the Dark Ages Sorcery rules, 5 pages of new Thaumaturgy, 5 pages of new Koldunism, and 3 pages of Necromancy. Dread Names, Red List? Let's put in about ten pages of new Thaumaturgy and Dark Thaumaturgy. Lore of the Clans? Gotta have more Necromancy, Abyss Mysticism, and Du'An Ki. Rites of the Blood? Hell with it. Let's give the anarchs their own form of blood sorcery while we're at it. DAV20...let's make the space dedicated to the 5 forms of blood sorcery half as long as the space dedicated to <b>25 other Disciplines. </b><br /> <br /> Would you take a bet whether or not there's new blood sorcery in the new ghouls book? (There isn't, but admit it. You didn't want to take that bet).<br /> <br /> Every new book comes out, you have tons more options for a any Tremere or Cappadocians/Giovanni/Nagaraja, or that tiny sliver of the Lasombra who are said to practice Abyss Mysticism, or that tiny sliver of Setites that do Anku, or the tiny sliver of Tzimisce that do Koldunism, or that less than half of the Assamites that do Dur'an Ki.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile, your average Brujah or Toreador or Ventrue is just like &quot;New level of Presence. I guess I&quot;ll take the effect that scares people. It's either that, or the effect that scares people.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I seem to have acquired a site for running play by post games. This is unexpected and frightening and come watch either the glorious play or the magnificent train wreck:<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://madnessforums.com/forums/index.php\" target=\"_blank\">The Malkavian Madness Network</a>","edited":{"userid":1515,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1515-benjcano","user":"BenjCano","date":". 12-25-2016, 07:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1515-benjcano","name":"BenjCano","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1515_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1276"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-25T17:32:45-08:00","id":1022145,"title":"","content":"Cry some more you filthy magic deficient scum<br /> <br /> *laughingtremere.jpg*<br /> <br /> OT: I have no strong feelings about Thaumaturgy and magic in general being as expanded as they do, It's always been a big fan favourite and it's the easy receptacle to put something cool an author comes up with (although the direction they took Abyss Mysticism fucking baffles me in this book).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12487-cantankerous-bees","name":"Cantankerous Bees","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"60"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-25T17:50:01-08:00","id":1022154,"title":"","content":"As far as I know schools of blood magic aren't cross compatible, so more options for Akhu or Setite Sorcerery isn't more options for Tremere.<br /> <br /> I think the issue with the blood magic inflation in general is that they want to add new powers, but only the framework of blood magic ever supported that. The first 5 levels of every normal discipline are concrete, and creating a new discipline either requires a new clan/bloodline, or some weird inceptor stuff. And I don't think I've ever seen an inceptor discipline actually printed.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11512-zanos","name":"Zanos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11512_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"550"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-25T22:34:58-08:00","id":1022231,"title":"","content":"I do wish the developers could spread some of the love around as combo disciplines rather than making <i>everything</i> a new Path or Ritual.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-25T23:50:56-08:00","id":1022238,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BenjCano</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/998155-v20-dark-ages-tome-of-secrets-discussion?p=1021767#post1021767\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just for fun, I did a little analysis. Here's how the space usage of ToS breaks down:<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://i.gyazo.com/47257dab7c8ec836aa95e7e8c94638e7.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> So...I'm seeing a lot of Thaumaturgy creep. When more than 52% of a supplement is dedicated to expanding the capabilities of blood sorcery, you can clearly see where the focus of the writers is.</div> </div> </div> </div>Something needed. Since the V20 Dark Ages reviewed all Kuldonismo system, necromancy but mainly from Sorceries Setites and Assamite.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/641-ben-linus","name":"Ben Linus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"444"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-26T08:27:56-08:00","id":1022351,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Gentleman Gamer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/998155-v20-dark-ages-tome-of-secrets-discussion?p=1000182#post1000182\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My intention with that section (where Koldunic Sorcerers jealously guard their power) stems back to Tzimisce territoriality, the idea of the crotchety old mage in his tower, and to act as a reason for Tzimisce disunity when opposing the more organised and cohesive Tremere. I feel it stands up.</div> </div> </div> </div>Though this post is seven weeks old, i only read it just now and feel compelled the reply to it now.<br /> <br /> As an explanation of Tzimisce disunity that section manages to be both wrong and unnecessary. It's wrong because <i>most Tzimisce are not Kolduns</i>, so establishing that the Kolduns don't get along with each other fails to explain the behaviour of the rest of the clan. It's unnecessary because it was already established that vampires in general are factitious and prone to infighting, with Tzimisce Voivoides in particular being a jealous and territorial lot who see each other as their only true rivals, and everyone else as nothing more than temporary inconveniences. The Tremere on the other hand have themselves been established as a highly unified clan with a rigid top-down structure. That the Tzimisce would take a long time to present a unified front and the Tremere would do so from the beginning is both self-evident, and detailed in every source on the Omen War. No further explanation is necessary.<br /> <br /> That's not the worst part though, the worst part is that this makes it very difficult to actually play a Koldun. A crotchety old mage in his tower is an NPC archetype that is very difficulty to do as a PC. Honestly this is a problem that affects the whole Kraina system, it really feels like it's meant for non-player characters, which is rather unlike the version of Koldunic sorcery presented in Player's Guide to the High Clans and reprinted in V20. The Krainas had interesting ideas, like the notion that each region has its native Koldunic path, and that each Koldun finds it easiest to invoke the path of their homeland, but the execution left a lot to be desired. Making path weaker outside their region of origin, for example, is something that doesn't affect NPCs who are likely stay in one place, but absolutely affects PCs who are likely to move from place to place. Also i honestly found some of the powers somewhat underwhelming.<br /> <br /> The mechanics of Koldunic Rivalry are what really makes Kolduns unplayable. Vampire is a game that rewards patience and planning, so your sorcery forcing you to immediately attack your rivals directly is tantamount to your sorcery forcing you to commit suicide. Seriously, what kind of self-respecting Koldun makes a beeline for a rival source of power, instead of enacting long term plan to bring the opposing Koldun to heel and <i>then</i> forcing their secrets out of them?<br /> <br /> Frankly the whole thing was just executed in an extremely clumsy way. If you had simply written mechanics through which one Koldun could steal knowledge from another, then jealousies and rivalries would develop all on their own. Just like the mere existence of Diablerie makes low-gen vampires fear high-gen vampires and seek to control them. There's no need to have mechanics making vampires roll Willpower every time they see a lower generation vampire, or risk frenzy every time they witness an advanced discipline power. No, the mere fact that those things can be stolen by devouring someone's soul is all the incentive vampires need to drive millenia of conflict. The same principle could have been applied to Kolduns, and it would have been both more interesting and more player friendly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1450,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1450-lys","user":"Lys","date":". 12-26-2016, 11:45 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1450-lys","name":"Lys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1450_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"480"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-26T11:11:10-08:00","id":1022398,"title":"","content":"So I've read Dark Thaumaturgy chapter and it's pretty bad. In a lot of ways. Let's go through the path to see exactly what's bad about it!<br /> <b>Fluff</b><br /> Retcons is the name of the day! Apparently blood magic is morally wrong because witchcraft is wrong. This is a rather bizarre surprise to spring on us at this point. Witchcraft was okay when Mage did it and it was okay for the entirety of VtM's original run but now it's suddenly bad?<br /> Next, Ur-Shulgi has been an infernalist all along! I told you guys that Assamites are an evil satanic cult, but no one ever listens.<br /> Next, more Setite fapping.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Setites despise Dark Thaumaturgy. As a clan devoted to their cults, families, and worshipers, they give would-be thaumaturgists advice on what deal may be good or bad. Serpents excel in earning the trust of other Cainites, though their counter-deals are said to carry as many conditions as those with demons. </div> </div> </div>I'd understand if this said &quot;Setites despise Dark Thaumaturgy because worshiping people other than Set is not kosher within Set's religion&quot;, but apparently it's because Setites know thaum too well? And don't Ventrue and Toreador, the original social clans, also excel in earning the trust of other Cainites? And for that matter, don't Tremere? You know, the clan that brokered the biggest vampire alliance ever? The clan that's actually in a vampire alliance <i>unlike Setites</i>?<br /> Next, new Dark Thaum nerf, as if it needed any. Dark Thaumaturgy can now be resisted with dif 9 willpower rolls, so it basically either doesn't work or critically succeeds as the target botches its roll.<br /> <br /> <b>&quot;Die Heriroschaft des Wyrm&quot;</b><br /> First things first: &quot;Heriroschaft&quot; is not a real word. German word for &quot;tyranny&quot; is &quot;die Tyrannei&quot; or &quot;die Gewaltherrschaft&quot;.<br /> Aaaand it only took two paragraphs into the introduction for someone to botch their writing roll!<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The zettler\u2019s recent disappearance, and other Cainites\u2019 subsequent discovery of his perfectly preserved scrolls detailing the Path, has led to a boutade of intrepid infernalists arising in the area. </div> </div> </div>Didn't you asshole wrote a page ago that the only way to learn Dark Thaum is from a demon? How are people learning it from scrolls?<br /> The path's &quot;price&quot; is really not a price at all. The first part where you can roll Wits + Occult is meaningless, because no one will ever roll 5 successes on dif 10 roll.<br /> The second part where a person with True Faith can cancel out your spells is also meaningless, because the books keep hammering in how extremely rare the people with True Faith are.<br /> <br /> <i>Malfean Infection</i><br /> No one ever will be excited to have this power. This is like &quot;give impotence to a green-eyed blonde chinese transvestite&quot;. So you are just going to use it maybe once per campaign if you remember that it exists. But even if you do use this power - it doesn't work. This power doesn't remove the True Faith from the person, only its powers, so the person can just bless themselves whenever and be free of your dreadful curse.<br /> <br /> <i>Bane to the Soul</i><br /> Are these the WtA Banes or not? If I got a WtA werewolf into the game, can they enter Umbra and punch the demon? Would their gifts work?<br /> Not a terrible power overall, for provoking frenzy and pyrophobia.<br /> <br /> <i>Dissonant Miserere</i><br /> There's a name that flows right off your tongue.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Through chanting, incantation, and inspired clack, the infernalist penetrates her victim\u2019s mind with the endless toiling noise of her ravings. </div> </div> </div>Through chanting that lasts one round that it takes you to activate the Discipline. Demons like brevity, I guess.<br /> Fairly nasty power, although I don't know how the victim is supposed to know that they can ask the demon to go away. Is that an innate knowledge they get when the ritual activates?<br /> Also does the victim have any hearing penalties for the fact that there's a constant demonic rock concert going around? You'd expect that, but I guess it's only willpower.<br /> <br /> <i>Feed the Wyrm</i><br /> Who takes the aggravated damage? The text implies that it's the thaumaturge, but I suspect that the intent was for the victim to be damaged.<br /> Appearance does nothing and this is Dark Ages where no one sees shit without a torch anyway, so you might as well live with your tumors instead of selling out to Wyrm.<br /> Does this thing work on Lasombra? They don't have reflections and the demon is supposed to appear in the mirror.<br /> <br /> <i>House the Maeljin</i><br /> Oooh baby! Free dots in any discipline for the low low price of roleplaying an asshole? Sold. I'm playing a vampire anyway.<br /> Do the Maeljin dots stack with existing dots or do you only get dots 1 and 2? Can I get elder disciplines from Maeljin? Level 11 disciplines?<br /> <img src=\"http://i.imgur.com/C1A6g8b.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> This time table is nuts. Why doesn't this use the same time table the previous powers did? Who'd want to kill their buddy only for nothing to happen because this was the end of the scene? Why does it go from One Week to Heat Death Of The Universe?<br /> <br /> <b>Rego Calatio</b><br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> God punishes us for everything. Open yourself, and let the devil inside!<br /> \u2014 Ahab the Traitor, infernalist Salubri of the wilds </div> </div> </div>So is this a canon statement that Ahab definitely exists and is not just a Salubri legend? This statement implies that Ahab is Christian - did he convert in the last two thousand years?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> A demon summoned by Rego Calatio remains on Earth until the sun rises, or it hears church bells. </div> </div> </div>Apparently I need to invest into a supply of ear plugs for my demonic army or move into Syria. <br /> Why don't the nightmares from the Price segment use Nightmares flaw rules?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> System: Each level of this Discipline requires the sacrifice of another being\u2019s life, the majority of demons requiring the death of an innocent in a circle of bloodied bones. </div> </div> </div>What does the minority require? Demon summoning is effectively random, how do I tell in advance what I need? Also cats are pretty inocent, can I sacrifice cats or is this supposed to be human-only thing?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11891-rumata","name":"Rumata","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11891_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"602"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-26T13:06:46-08:00","id":1022433,"title":"","content":"Another eyebrow-raising moment in the section on Dark Thaumaturgy:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Demonic Patron (5 pt. Supernatural Merit)</b><br /> Your actions drew the attention of a demonic entity. Maybe you deliberately sought it as a means to gain power, or perhaps it wheedled its way into your existence and now won\u2019t let go. The entity became a patron of yours, offering guidance when sought and assistance against your foes. One night it will turn on you and demand something. You will be unable to refuse its request. Until that time, your patron counts as three dots in Mentor and two dots in Allies. </div> </div> </div>So, for five freebie points you could purchase supernatural patronage, which provides you with the equivalent of three dots in Mentor and two dots in Allies, but which will eventually screw you over...<br /> <br /> ... or you could just spend those five freebie points on the three dots in Mentor and two dots in Allies.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/317-james_willoughby","name":"James_Willoughby","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar317_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-26T13:48:42-08:00","id":1022441,"title":"","content":"I appreciate the irony of being on the receiving end of &quot;be careful what you wish for&quot; but the Koldunic Sorcery section was such a disappointment. It's . . . . okay if you're an NPC badass who already has his own domain and lots of power and resources but terrible for a PC to try and get much use out of. There are interesting ideas in there, but they're wasted in a rules structure that is hostile to PC use. The inclusion of unnecessary hostility mechanics just makes it worse. Kolduns are a minority among the Tzimisce so it shouldn't affect the Clan as a whole and we already have Tzimisce territoriality (which is thematically linked to their Clan weakness) with rival neighboring broods and the Carpathian-Dracon split to account for their disunity (and that's without bringing up the so-called Old Clan).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11489-cynical-cat","name":"Cynical Cat","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"33"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-26T18:33:01-08:00","id":1022567,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rumata</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/998155-v20-dark-ages-tome-of-secrets-discussion?p=1022398#post1022398\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Didn't you asshole wrote a page ago that the only way to learn Dark Thaum is from a demon?</div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:red\">I <i>know</i> I don't need to explain to you that calling people assholes is against rule 1.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-26T19:10:15-08:00","id":1022579,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rumata</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/998155-v20-dark-ages-tome-of-secrets-discussion?p=1022398#post1022398\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Next, Ur-Shulgi has been an infernalist all along! I told you guys that Assamites are an evil satanic cult, but no one ever listens.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, it was a dead giveaway even when Ur-Shulgi first appeared in a WW supplement years ago.The Tremere curse, which was powerful enough to override the Baali curse gets tossed away effortlessly, yet the weaker and previously nullified Baali curse remained. Hmmm, Ur-Shugli didn't remove both of the curses WHY?. Oh, and the Baali were sired by Saulot, who not coincidentally happens to be in Tremere's body...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5853-krb","name":"KRB","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"275"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-26T19:22:39-08:00","id":1022582,"title":"","content":"Well given that Ur-Shulgi is a genocidal diablerie fanatic, I don't see why he would want to get rid of the &quot;more of my Clan is compelled to follow the agenda I'm commanding!&quot; curse even if he could.<br /> <br /> Of course as all the other original Clans have in-built weaknesses, I'm not sure I believe the underlying Assamite weakness only originated in a Baali Curse.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-26T19:32:07-08:00","id":1022585,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KRB</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/998155-v20-dark-ages-tome-of-secrets-discussion?p=1022579#post1022579\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, it was a dead giveaway even when Ur-Shulgi . . .<br /> . . . and the Baali were sired by Saulot. . .</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh really. . .","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://t0.gstatic.com/images?q=tbn:ANd9GcTAO8runv-CR5dodCXgw_8wdJype5yunYCODWdZiBAwUP5WFVv8\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://ksr-ugc.imgix.net/assets/003/593/392/92a29c2836b988505781770a32720148_original.png?v=1428699067&amp;w=700&amp;h=&amp;fit=max&amp;auto=format&amp;lossless=true&amp;s=69ffdde357a0cdd88ee89934622443f9\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img692/7017/hh2support.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img703/6636/6kvo.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1721-beckett","name":"Beckett","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1721_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1077"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-27T08:04:19-08:00","id":1022761,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rumata</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/998155-v20-dark-ages-tome-of-secrets-discussion?p=1022398#post1022398\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>&quot;Die Heriroschaft des Wyrm&quot;</b><br /> First things first: &quot;Heriroschaft&quot; is not a real word. German word for &quot;tyranny&quot; is &quot;die Tyrannei&quot; or &quot;die Gewaltherrschaft&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Probably the most bothersome part is that this was noted in the errata thread.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12552-monalfie","name":"Monalfie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12552_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-27T09:22:33-08:00","id":1022796,"title":"","content":"I really found the new powers flavorful and in keeping with the setting. Sure they're not for everyone and sure there are made up words but Mytherceriia is a made up word and not for every game either. I think the reason I really liked the powers in this book was because I could visualize a use for every one of them that would really make a story interesting. Every power has a little story behind it. That's fantastic!<br /> <br /> Maybe this is an unpopular opinion but I think this is one of the most interesting Vampire books I've read.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3241-stannis","name":"Stannis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3241_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"115"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-29T06:49:54-08:00","id":1023731,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Monalfie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/998155-v20-dark-ages-tome-of-secrets-discussion?p=1022761#post1022761\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Probably the most bothersome part is that this was noted in the errata thread.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I'm not sure why that wasn't changed. In my defence, a German friend of mine said it would be the word appropriate to the era and region, so it's the one I used, but I'm not sure why it wasn't picked up from the errata comment.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#000080\">Matthew Dawkins</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000080\">In-House Developer for Onyx Path Publishing</span></b><br /> <br /> <i><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b><span style=\"color:#008080\">Website: </span><a href=\"http://www.matthewdawkins.com\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.matthewdawkins.com</span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#008080\">Patreon: </span><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins</span></a></b></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/152-the-gentleman-gamer","name":"The Gentleman Gamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar152_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-30T07:03:22-08:00","id":1024292,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Monalfie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/998155-v20-dark-ages-tome-of-secrets-discussion?p=1022761#post1022761\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Probably the most bothersome part is that this was noted in the errata thread.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Actually it has been changed to Herrschaft.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#000080\">Matthew Dawkins</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000080\">In-House Developer for Onyx Path Publishing</span></b><br /> <br /> <i><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b><span style=\"color:#008080\">Website: </span><a href=\"http://www.matthewdawkins.com\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.matthewdawkins.com</span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#008080\">Patreon: </span><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins</span></a></b></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/152-the-gentleman-gamer","name":"The Gentleman Gamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar152_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-30T07:25:07-08:00","id":1024303,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/998155-v20-dark-ages-tome-of-secrets-discussion?p=1022351#post1022351\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As an explanation of Tzimisce disunity that section manages to be both wrong and unnecessary. It's wrong because <i>most Tzimisce are not Kolduns</i>, so establishing that the Kolduns don't get along with each other fails to explain the behaviour of the rest of the clan. It's unnecessary because it was already established that vampires in general are factitious and prone to infighting, with Tzimisce Voivoides in particular being a jealous and territorial lot who see each other as their only true rivals, and everyone else as nothing more than temporary inconveniences. The Tremere on the other hand have themselves been established as a highly unified clan with a rigid top-down structure. That the Tzimisce would take a long time to present a unified front and the Tremere would do so from the beginning is both self-evident, and detailed in every source on the Omen War. No further explanation is necessary.<br /> <br /> That's not the worst part though, the worst part is that this makes it very difficult to actually play a Koldun. A crotchety old mage in his tower is an NPC archetype that is very difficulty to do as a PC. Honestly this is a problem that affects the whole Kraina system, it really feels like it's meant for non-player characters, which is rather unlike the version of Koldunic sorcery presented in Player's Guide to the High Clans and reprinted in V20. The Krainas had interesting ideas, like the notion that each region has its native Koldunic path, and that each Koldun finds it easiest to invoke the path of their homeland, but the execution left a lot to be desired. Making path weaker outside their region of origin, for example, is something that doesn't affect NPCs who are likely stay in one place, but absolutely affects PCs who are likely to move from place to place. Also i honestly found some of the powers somewhat underwhelming.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I'm saddened that you really dislike the Koldunism as presented in Tome of Secrets.<br /> <br /> While I agree that vampires are by nature fractious, I've heard a lot of people ask &quot;how is it that the small number of Tremere possibly withstood the Tzimisce?&quot; over the years. This is one such reason. While not every Tzimisce is a Koldun, perhaps this explains why there are so few of them. Their unity - if possible - would be a fantastic weapon for the Voivodate to wield. The Koldun are an opportunity for Rustovitch, if he can get them working in concert for the first time in centuries. That - for me - is the start of an interesting chronicle.<br /> <br /> Note that the kraina compulsion is to &quot;accumulate further power.&quot; It doesn't mean they automatically kill one another, especially if the rites and powers are taught freely. The only time frenzy is risked is when another sorcerer practices an unknown kraina within sight of the protagonist.<br /> <br /> NPC Koldun may well be tower-bound sorcerers, but there's no reason players can't all take on the roles of travelling sorcerers, if they so wish. Bear in mind that if they're open with each other, like the Many-Headed Seekers described in the book, none of this fractious behaviour occurs.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#000080\">Matthew Dawkins</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000080\">In-House Developer for Onyx Path Publishing</span></b><br /> <br /> <i><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b><span style=\"color:#008080\">Website: </span><a href=\"http://www.matthewdawkins.com\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.matthewdawkins.com</span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#008080\">Patreon: </span><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins</span></a></b></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/152-the-gentleman-gamer","name":"The Gentleman Gamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar152_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-30T07:28:44-08:00","id":1024304,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>James_Willoughby</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/998155-v20-dark-ages-tome-of-secrets-discussion?p=1022433#post1022433\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, for five freebie points you could purchase supernatural patronage, which provides you with the equivalent of three dots in Mentor and two dots in Allies, but which will eventually screw you over...<br /> <br /> ... or you could just spend those five freebie points on the three dots in Mentor and two dots in Allies.</div> </div> </div> </div>You've got it completely right - this is the equivalent of those Backgrounds, but this one is a combination of the two with a little flavour behind it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#000080\">Matthew Dawkins</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000080\">In-House Developer for Onyx Path Publishing</span></b><br /> <br /> <i><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b><span style=\"color:#008080\">Website: </span><a href=\"http://www.matthewdawkins.com\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.matthewdawkins.com</span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#008080\">Patreon: </span><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins</span></a></b></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/152-the-gentleman-gamer","name":"The Gentleman Gamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar152_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-30T07:29:58-08:00","id":1024306,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Gentleman Gamer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/998155-v20-dark-ages-tome-of-secrets-discussion?p=1024292#post1024292\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Actually it has been changed to Herrschaft.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, my apologies, in that case. I was going off what Rumata said. So I'm not sure what part he saw it wrong at. Maybe he was referencing the backer version? Glad to hear it was seen regardless.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12552-monalfie","name":"Monalfie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12552_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-30T07:38:06-08:00","id":1024313,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Monalfie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/998155-v20-dark-ages-tome-of-secrets-discussion?p=1024306#post1024306\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh, my apologies, in that case. I was going off what Rumata said. So I'm not sure what part he saw it wrong at. Maybe he was referencing the backer version? Glad to hear it was seen regardless.</div> </div> </div> </div>Possibly, though I've got the updated backer version and it has been corrected, so who knows.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#000080\">Matthew Dawkins</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000080\">In-House Developer for Onyx Path Publishing</span></b><br /> <br /> <i><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b><span style=\"color:#008080\">Website: </span><a href=\"http://www.matthewdawkins.com\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.matthewdawkins.com</span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#008080\">Patreon: </span><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins</span></a></b></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/152-the-gentleman-gamer","name":"The Gentleman Gamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar152_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-30T15:22:21-08:00","id":1024516,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Gentleman Gamer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/998155-v20-dark-ages-tome-of-secrets-discussion?p=1024304#post1024304\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You've got it completely right - this is the equivalent of those Backgrounds, but this one is a combination of the two with a little flavour behind it.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's not quite true; Demonic Patron is a five-point Merit, equivalent to five Background points, but with an added disadvantage. It is, in game terms, quantifiably worse than merely purchasing the Backgrounds granted to your character by the Merit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/317-james_willoughby","name":"James_Willoughby","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar317_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-31T03:00:51-08:00","id":1024690,"title":"","content":"From a mechanical standpoint. There are players that might regard the added story potential of the strings attached as a feature rather than a bug.<br /> <br /> Gentleman Gamer, in general I enjoy your work, and appreciate the grace and propriety with which you interact with folks on the forum. However, based on what I've read, I must sadly conclude that this book and particularly its take on Koldunic Sorcery is not for me. Perhaps not a huge surprise since DAV20 in general has been a big pile of Do Not Want from my perspective, but I'd hoped that subsequent products dealing with that subsystem would make it <i>more</i> palatable rather than <i>less</i>. (My principal VtM character is a koldun from an old Black Hand chronicle, and the grafting of the DAV system into the modern day for that supplement means I either have to rebuild my character to his detriment holding my nose the whole while, or accept that he is now a benighted dupe of Kupula.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-31T04:26:03-08:00","id":1024707,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Matt the Bruins fan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/998155-v20-dark-ages-tome-of-secrets-discussion?p=1024690#post1024690\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">From a mechanical standpoint. There are players that might regard the added story potential of the strings attached as a feature rather than a bug.<br /> <br /> Gentleman Gamer, in general I enjoy your work, and appreciate the grace and propriety with which you interact with folks on the forum. However, based on what I've read, I must sadly conclude that this book and particularly its take on Koldunic Sorcery is not for me. Perhaps not a huge surprise since DAV20 in general has been a big pile of Do Not Want from my perspective, but I'd hoped that subsequent products dealing with that subsystem would make it <i>more</i> palatable rather than <i>less</i>. (My principal VtM character is a koldun from an old Black Hand chronicle, and the grafting of the DAV system into the modern day for that supplement means I either have to rebuild my character to his detriment holding my nose the whole while, or accept that he is now a benighted dupe of Kupula.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you for the kind words. I'm obviously disappointed you don't like the book, and that the powers don't serve your roleplay as you'd like. The good news is there are now several takes on Koldunism you can use. The bad news is this one doesn't work for you.<br /> <br /> I sincerely hope you find my future work a little more palatable. Here's to upcoming books!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#000080\">Matthew Dawkins</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000080\">In-House Developer for Onyx Path Publishing</span></b><br /> <br /> <i><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b><span style=\"color:#008080\">Website: </span><a href=\"http://www.matthewdawkins.com\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.matthewdawkins.com</span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#008080\">Patreon: </span><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins</span></a></b></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/152-the-gentleman-gamer","name":"The Gentleman Gamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar152_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-31T04:30:59-08:00","id":1024708,"title":"","content":"In terms of &quot;what to do&quot;, with all of this said and done...<br /> <br /> In DA I would allow players to make the decisions, with my guidance. If they really want a close relationship with Fire Spirits, I can say that their Koldunic experience begins with a hot spring resting over a bed of microvolcanic activity, and let them have Way of Fire. If they really want a close relationship with a Forest, not a specific element, I would let them design a Kraina by combining 5 existing Kraina and Way powers into a progression which matches their environment.<br /> <br /> In Modern Nights I would use a similar system, but the Ways are far more common and Kraina are exceptionally rare. Some have even grown feeble since the place they were born from has grown feeble. Imagine a Koldun who took up residence in the forests of the English Midlands... their powers would have waned exceptionally, forcing them to swap over to Ways. On the offchance of this ever happening to a PC I would &quot;refund&quot; them their dots in Ways with a very, very small penalty (liquefy the dead Kraina and give them 90% of the EXP back to put into Ways).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-29T10:08:12-08:00","id":1040073,"title":"","content":"I liked the way that blood magics and things were handled in Tome of Secrets, but as of writing this I'm playing a Lasombra Abyss Mystic, and I found that section lacking a little. It all felt like it was built with an antagonist and chronicle in mind, rather than a player.<br /> <br /> The first two rituals were pretty much useless, since there isn't quite a definition of a &quot;true mystic&quot; and oubliettes are supposed to be about as rare as mystics are.<br /> Abyssal Blade is an interesting concept, though armor doesn't contribute more than 5 dots to a person's soak rating, with a -3 penalty to dexterity. The agg damage to mortals is alright, but they'll probably die anyways if a vampire is attacking them. Agg damage to vampires, however...<br /> Implant the Bezoar is nice, kinda op considering there's not really a chance for the victim to resist the Bezoar and it starts draining crazy amounts of blood after only a few nights.<br /> One With the Dark is another interesting concept, one that seems designed with the player in mind, perhaps. The appearance boost is a little strange, but I'll roll with it. Summoning the Blatherskites, also cool, a little tedious but worth it for the slaughter that comes after.<br /> Angra Mainyu Consumes Spenta Mainyu is definitely a cool ritual. I absolutely love how crazy it is, throwing up darkness-tar that puts out all lights in an area and doesn't allow them to light back up? Inspiring.<br /> Lord Aludian's Orifices is a unique one. I don't usually play games where the sexy-times come into play, but if people want to use it, that's their thing. It certainly gave me a giggle.<br /> Boukephos' Gateway gives me maybe the most trouble and the most joy out of them all. This is another one I thought was an amazing concept, but not very well executed. Yes, it's hardcore with those 2 conviction rolls, but you better have lots of conviction or this is destined to fail. Not only that, if you fail, you can't get on the Road of the Abyss? Not fun, especially for a mystic using One With the Dark. That -1 blood on all obtenebration abilities, tho.<br /> Beckon the Ingurgitant, great ritual, clever usage can lead to lots of murder, I like it.<br /> Boukephos' Chosen Oubliette is a little silly, another ritual that seems like it's designed for NPCs to attack PCs with. Not to mention it's a level 9 ritual, so unless you're Lasombra you don't have much hope of attempting this.<br /> <br /> The oubliette background is pretty cool, I'd only ever buy up to level 3, but then again anything passed that is something that the writer seems to have handcrafted for a chronicle to be done in. It's the same for a few of the denizens of the Abyss as well, people like the Umbriferous Man and the Minacious Legion.<br /> <br /> All in all, I'll probably cherry pick one or two rituals out of this book for Abyss Mystics, and then look elsewhere. Sorry for the giant paragraph, this is my first post and I have lots to say about Tome of Secrets. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12928-leoblood","name":"LeoBlood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12928_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-29T11:38:24-08:00","id":1040117,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12928-leoblood\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12928_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12928\" data-vbnamecard=\"12928\">LeoBlood</a><br /> \u200bAgg damage to mortals is actually meaningless. Mortals don't make distinction between lethal and aggravated damage. Abyssal Blade also doesn't deal agg to vampires and doesn't bypass Fortitude, so its effects are highly questionable.<br /> One With the Dark is full of problems. It never explains what a &quot;master Mystic&quot; is, where you learn &quot;language of the Abyss&quot;, how do you tattoo your body when all appearance changes go away the next night, who are the &quot;Cainites named in the ritual&quot;. The whole thing is basically unusable without a full rewrite.<br /> Summoning the Blatherskites starts with an extremely derpy &quot;Mystics publicly snub those who practice this ritual&quot;. Abyss Mystics are an extreme minority of the clan Lasombra, who are a minority of the general Vampire group which in itself is a minority of humanity. We are three levels of minority deep and are basically talking about being snubbed by the other two members of the school's anime club because you said you like Naruto.<br /> Boukephos' Gateway is either too risky to ever use or has no danger at all. If the failure penalty doesn't affect vampires who are already on the Road of the Abyss, then you (under the supervision of your sire) do the ritual until you succeed and there are no stakes. If the failure penalty does affect the mystics, then you never try the Gateway because the price of failure is setting your concept on fire and making a new character.<br /> <br /> Oubliette is the background I just don't get. It doesn't work as a defense for your spooky mansion because effects take hold only after you spend days in it. On top of that, being an owner of Oubliette doesn't make you immune to the effects so you can never get the xp discount - you lose 1 WP each night and you need to spend 20 nights. Unless the Oubliette is filled with roleplaying props for you to milk Nature/Demeanor - you aer fucked.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12892-kammerer","name":"Kammerer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12892_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-29T16:38:56-08:00","id":1040284,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12892-kammerer\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12892_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12892\" data-vbnamecard=\"12892\">Kammerer</a> Shall we stop pretending that anything was ever balanced or well-written mechanically? I LOVE VTM and I love the system presented, but Disciplines and Blood Magic are more a case of finding stuff you can keep then finding stuff to fix. Serpentis 1, Dominate 1, Presence 2 are all If My Roll Works You Are Screwed, and they are not alone. There are horrible mechanical mistakes in this book, and it might be marginally worse than others RE balance and functionally written powers, but it's not unique or special in this regard IMO.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-29T16:43:34-08:00","id":1040288,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/998155-v20-dark-ages-tome-of-secrets-discussion?p=1040284#post1040284\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12892-kammerer\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12892_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12892\" data-vbnamecard=\"12892\">Kammerer</a> Shall we stop pretending that anything was ever balanced or well-written mechanically? I LOVE VTM and I love the system presented, but Disciplines and Blood Magic are more a case of finding stuff you can keep then finding stuff to fix. Serpentis 1, Dominate 1, Presence 2 are all If My Roll Works You Are Screwed, and they are not alone. There are horrible mechanical mistakes in this book, and it might be marginally worse than others RE balance and functionally written powers, but it's not unique or special in this regard IMO.</div> </div> </div> </div>Eh? I haven't really talked about balance of powers here. My only mechanical complaint was about Boukephos' Gateway, and that's that the power is too risky to ever use.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12892-kammerer","name":"Kammerer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12892_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-29T17:20:41-08:00","id":1040308,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kammerer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/998155-v20-dark-ages-tome-of-secrets-discussion?p=1040288#post1040288\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Eh? I haven't really talked about balance of powers here. My only mechanical complaint was about Boukephos' Gateway, and that's that the power is too risky to ever use.</div> </div> </div> </div>I misspoke. I mean the powers are quite often poorly written. Neat ideas, but the fluff is weird and doesn't match other fluff, and the fluff doesn't match the mechanics... I love VTM for the overall System and for the Lore which is amazing! And I love VTM for some of its powers. But you don't have to go too far to find powers with bad fluff or bad mechanics. And when you go obscure, you get crazy shit like Dark Thaumaturgy turning people and Vampires into a cat. Like, an actual cat. That sort of thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-29T18:10:28-08:00","id":1040333,"title":"","content":"That's hardly an excuse for bad writing, is it? I understand why V20 doesn't change the tire fire that is its core mechanic - because it's a nostalgia product and remaking the game is not the point. But I don't see that as a defense for new powers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12892-kammerer","name":"Kammerer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12892_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-30T05:58:16-08:00","id":1040600,"title":"","content":"@Kammerer<br /> <br /> We may be too many minorities deep, but remember that the Road of the Abyss encourages mystics to keep in contact with one another. <br /> Also, this is the last sentence in the book on Oubliettes: The Oubliette\u2019s owner is attuned to <br /> the dungeon, and therefore suffers no ill effects within it.<br /> <br /> I don't know if that makes the Oubliette useless for its owner to get that exp discount, or just means that they sit in the dark perfectly unharmed for a month, but that's the book. <br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12928-leoblood","name":"LeoBlood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12928_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-30T06:05:03-08:00","id":1040605,"title":"","content":"That makes it even weirder. Oubliette background is essentially 1 freebie in exchange for a 1xp discount on all your future AM purchases. Wat? This can't possibly be the intention.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12892-kammerer","name":"Kammerer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12892_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-30T07:00:32-08:00","id":1040638,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kammerer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/998155-v20-dark-ages-tome-of-secrets-discussion?p=1040605#post1040605\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That makes it even weirder. Oubliette background is essentially 1 freebie in exchange for a 1xp discount on all your future AM purchases. Wat? This can't possibly be the intention.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not only that, but if you make it big enough, you can perform some rituals that require an oubliette or an otherwise strange location, like summoning the blatherskites and bezoars in pools of dark water/subterranean lakes. It's a bit damning to see such a glaring problem.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12928-leoblood","name":"LeoBlood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12928_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-01-12T13:49:24-08:00","id":1547701,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Boukephos' Chosen Oubliette is a little silly, another ritual that seems like it's designed for NPCs to attack PCs with. Not to mention it's a level 9 ritual, so unless you're Lasombra you don't have much hope of attempting this. </div> </div> </div>It's silly, not because it's &quot;designed for NPCs (as we ST might be really interested in good advanced powers that could give a theme for a given story), the problem with Boukephos' Chosen Oubliette is that it's absolutely terrible for a level 9 power. There's no use for the power. Why would you give a village (hamlet, city, etc) a two way ticket to the Abyss!? There's no point to the power, no real benefit and it fails one of the most important aspects of an advanced power that it's to give this &quot;sense of dread and awe&quot; that a power that could be used only by a few characters in the entire world should give. It doesn't even kill the mortals, I mean, what!? You fail the (not so hard) WP test to get a two-way ticket to the Abyss and gain a derangement (oh wow!, so evil). I mean, in all honesty (and respect to whoever designed it) I fail to see the point of the power. I never really got this idea of powers to give people two-way tickets to the Abyss, if it was permanent and they would have to find a way back (which most wouldn't be able to) it would still be a somewhat lackluster power for a level 9, but as it is, I can't imagine any character ever wanting to perform this ritual...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}